{
  "raw": {
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/39C3B08FA765F09BC547D09C6AC939C8/jobs/79840": {
      "title": "Senior Project Coordinator - CETL (4199)",
      "description": "Senior Project Coordinator - CETL (4199) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Senior Project Coordinator - CETL (4199) Hot Job Main Campus - Marietta, GA 30060 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Staff Apply Description JOB DESCRIPTION Job Title: Project Coordinator FLSA Status: Non-Exempt Reports To: Director, Center for Excellence in Teaching and Learning Pay Grade: 15 Department: Center for Excellence in Teaching and Learning (CETL) Last Revision: 10/14/2024 Approved By: Human Resources Date: 10/14/2024 LIFE UNIVERSITY About Us Since 1974, Life University has been a trailblazer in postsecondary education, seeking individuals eager to join our team dedicated to shaping the future of health and wellness education. Situated in Marietta, Georgia, our university’s campus provides a nurturing, yet dynamic environment for academic and personal growth. We are a specialized institution focused on vitalistic education in the fields of healthcare, business administration, and the social sciences, providing a range of undergraduate and graduate degrees alongside our flagship Doctor of Chiropractic program. As we continue our mission to empower students and pioneer innovative approaches to vitalistic education, we are actively seeking passionate professionals to join us in our commitment to excellence. Serving Lasting Purpose At Life University, our mission extends beyond education—we strive to embody a Lasting Purpose: To Give, To Do, To Love, To Serve—out of your own abundance. Life University’s guiding principle is to live an inner-directed life, recognizing that the willingness and desire to serve your community and your fellow human beings are just as important as academic pursuits. This philosophy drives our commitment to our students, staff, and the broader community, inspiring us to make meaningful contributions to the world through the transformative power of education and service. We believe that everyone has unique gifts, and as a member of the global community, it is our duty to share those gifts generously, living by the principle of giving, doing, loving, and serving out of abundance. Equal Employment Opportunity Life University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We provide consideration for employment to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, disability, or protected veteran status. JOB PURPOSE The purpose of the Project Coordinator is to coordinate and oversees the planning process and monitors progress toward achieving long term and short-term project goals including support and assistance for faculty and staff development and training, data management, technology training, and other duties as requested. ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS Perform a variety of administrative duties, including financial tracking, managing information, purchasing, responding to inquiries, creating reports and spreadsheets, taking meeting minutes, etc. Plan and manage meetings, events, workshops, and campus-wide events for faculty and staff. Coordinate project planning for the department, including assessing needs, managing data, monitoring departmental timelines, etc. Create online, print, and electronic communications. Provide support to faculty and staff in the use of educational technologies. Additional duties and responsibilities as assigned. ADDITIONAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Assumes additional responsibilities and performs special projects as needed or requested. Exhibits student centeredness in performance of all job duties. Treats all others with respect; understands the impact of culture/background on the behavior of others; respects differences among the Life community and demonstrates inclusive behavior. Anticipates, listens to, understands and responds to customer needs. Delivers work products and services to customers in a way that reflects positively upon the department and the University. Qualifications REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS Education, Training, and/or Experience A Bachelors’ Degree from an accredited institution of higher education in Business Administration, or similar; AND Minimum of [three] (3) years of professional experience in an administrative environment. Strong computer and educational technology skills. Ability to be self-directed and work independently. Strong problem-solving skills. Ability to prioritize and complete projects and tasks on time. Effective oral and written communication skills. Ability to work effectively with a broad range of constituents in a diverse community. A combination of education and years of experience may be considered in lieu of the specified degree level requirement. Certifications, Licenses, Registrations None required. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Master’s Degree in Education or related field. Three ( 3+) years’ experience designing and facilitating training materials and resources for adult learners. Demonstrated experience in using and supporting others in the effective use of Blackboard or other learning management system. Effective oral and written presentation skills. PHYSICAL DEMANDS Nature of work requires an ability to operate standard business office equipment. Requires ability to communicate and exchange information, collects, compiles, compares, and prepares work documents, set-up and maintain work files. Must be able to lift up to 25 lbs; retrieving and placing materials on high shelves and on floor-level shelves; standing, walking; carrying; grasping; hearing; seeing; sitting; kneeling; climbing; balancing; stooping; crouching and reaching. WORKING CONDITIONS Work performed in a general office environment. May require some travel. This job description is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties or skills required for the job and is subject to review and change at any time, with or without notice, in accordance with the needs of Life University.  Since no job description can detail all the duties and responsibilities that may be required from time to time in the performance of a job, duties and responsibilities that may be inherent in a job, reasonably required for its performance, or required due to the changing nature of the job shall also be considered part of the jobholder’s responsibility. Share job details to About Life University Shape the future of health sciences and holistic education. Be part of a mission-driven team that values innovation and integrity. Apply today! Located in Marietta, GA, our 110-acre campus offers a collaborative environment for faculty and staff to innovate, educate, and serve. www.life.edu Join a team that empowers leaders to act with integrity and make a lasting impact on communities worldwide. Our Mission Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/39C3B08FA765F09BC547D09C6AC939C8/jobs/82007": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant II - CAAR (4429)",
      "description": "Administrative Assistant II - CAAR (4429) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Administrative Assistant II - CAAR (4429) Main Campus - Marietta, GA 30060 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Staff Apply Description Purpose Reports directly to the Executive Director of the Center of Academic Advisement and Retention. This position provides administrative support in a variety of functions to the individual team, department, and/or another group in the organization. Collects, reviews, and analyzes data and prepares reports, charts, budgets, and other presentation materials. Essential Job Functions Manage all event logistics, including scheduling, venue coordination, registrations, communications, materials, and on-site support. Provides all aspects of administrative support for departmental operations, including but not limited to answering phone calls and providing information about the programs within the department. Open and close department along with greeting vendors, customers, students, and other visitors in a friendly, approachable, and professional manner and ensures that they are escorted to the appropriate areas. Assists the Executive and Directors of the Center of Academic Advisement and Retention in the preparation of departmental reports; maintaining various databases and spreadsheets, including budgetary expenditures, income generated by the department. Ensures operation of equipment by completing preventive maintenance requirements; calling for repairs; maintaining equipment inventories. Assists the department employees with equipment and computer problems, typing of materials, etc. Maintains supplies inventory by checking stock to determine inventory level; anticipating needed supplies; placing and expediting orders for supplies; verifying receipt of supplies. Assists in data collection and review associated with the surveys of the University Advisement Center. Attends and maintains meeting minutes on all departmental meetings. Organizes and maintains department files both electronic and hard copy. Recruit, train, schedule, and supervise departmental work-study students. Provide executive-level administrative support to the Executive Director and departmental leadership, including calendar management, travel coordination, meeting scheduling, correspondence, and special projects. Maintains neat, clean, professional appearance as directed by university policy. Additional Duties And Responsibilities Assumes additional responsibilities and performs special projects as needed or directed. Qualifications Education, Training and/or Experience An A. S. Degree in Business Administration or equivalent; must have three (3) five (5) years of administrative support experience is required. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and Personal Characteristics Able to perform duties independently with minimal supervision. Basic math skills (addition, subtraction, multiplication and division). Ability to operate standard office equipment and follow office procedures. High degree of integrity; highly ethical. Must be able to work with diverse groups of individuals and have thorough knowledge of academic resource issues. Strong interpersonal skills: ability to deal with potentially difficult situations involving sensitive and confidential issues. Strong attention to detail; ability to organize work and perform duties with a high level of accuracy. Effective oral and written communication skills. Able to prioritize and manage multiple projects, adhering to strict timelines. Good communication and presentation skills. High degree of initiative and independent judgment. Well-developed analytical and problem-solving abilities. Able to organize work, engage in a variety of tasks simultaneously and consistently meet deadlines. Able to write reports, business correspondence. Strong Computer skills; data entry and spreadsheet software capabilities. Preferred Qualifications A bachelor's degree in Business Administration or a similar field is desired. Physical Demands Nature of work requires an ability to operate standard business office equipment. Requires ability to communicate and exchange information, collects, compiles, compares, and prepares work documents, set-up and maintain work files. Must spend majority of time concentrating on CRT identifying and updating information and performing data entry input. Must be able to lift up to 25 lbs; retrieving and placing materials on high shelves and on floor-level shelves; standing, walking; carrying; grasping; hearing; seeing; sitting; kneeling; climbing; balancing; stooping; crouching and reaching. Working Conditions Work performed in a general office environment. May require availability for overtime hours during peak periods. Share job details to About Life University Shape the future of health sciences and holistic education. Be part of a mission-driven team that values innovation and integrity. Apply today! Located in Marietta, GA, our 110-acre campus offers a collaborative environment for faculty and staff to innovate, educate, and serve. www.life.edu Join a team that empowers leaders to act with integrity and make a lasting impact on communities worldwide. Our Mission Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/39C3B08FA765F09BC547D09C6AC939C8/jobs/81575": {
      "title": "Student Advocate (4407)",
      "description": "Student Advocate (4407) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Student Advocate (4407) Main Campus - Marietta, GA 30060 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Staff Apply Description Purpose The Student Advocate I serves as the first point of contact and gateway to Financial Aid, Student Accounts, Registrar, Housing & Residential Life, Orientation, Graduation, Career Services, Disability Services, Counseling and The Office of Conflict Resolution and Accountability, Campus Activities, Student Organizations, Fitness Center, Intramurals and Campus Recreation.  This position is responsible for student “triage”: determining students’ needs and connecting them to the right department, person and services needed to navigate the college successfully. Essential Job Functions Provide exemplary levels of customer service to all students. Proactive in addressing student issues and concerns. Serve as” triage agent” in determining what services students are and how to address concerns. Accurately assesses each student’s situation to determine its urgency and proceeds appropriately. Receives documents required by Financial Aid, Registrar and Student Account, Housing, Disability Services and verifies the completeness of documents. Respond to general questions, scan departmental documents. Aid students using computer kiosks to complete forms, Life U website, Eaglenet and third-party websites related to Life University requests. Remain current with all academic policies and procedures. Cross functional support across the Student Affairs Division. Additional Duties And Responsibilities Exhibits student centeredness in performance of all job duties. Exhibits knowledge of and sensitivity to the interrelatedness of all student services departments. Treat others with respect, with the understanding of cultural differences, perspectives, awareness. Performs all work duties in an inclusive manner and perspective. Assumes additional responsibilities, performs special projects as needed or directed. Supports and assists the Office of Disability Services as a testing proctor. Qualifications Required Qualifications Education, Training and/or Experience Associate degree and one (1) year previous experience, OR High School Diploma/Equivalent AND three (3) years previous experience. Demonstrated experience with Microsoft Office, specifically Word, Excel and Outlook. Demonstrated track record of delivering superior customer service. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and Personal Characteristics Demonstrate integrity and professionalism in appearance and demeanor; ability to share and impart knowledge and reasoning to others under stressful conditions. Strong attention to detail, ability to organize work and perform duties with a high level of accuracy. Strong interpersonal skills, including oral and written communication skills, listening skills and team building and the ability to think critically. Knowledge of general office policies and procedures. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution of higher education. Familiarity with Ellucian’s Colleague. General familiarity with FERPA/HIPAA/ADA and basic Title IV and Georgia State financial aid programs. Physical Demands Nature of work requires an ability to operate standard business office equipment. Requires ability to communicate and exchange information, collecting, compiling, compares, and prepares work documents, set-up and maintain work files. Much time is spent concentrating on CRT identifying and updating information and performing some data entry. Must be able to lift 25 lbs., retrieving and placing materials on high shelves and on floor-level shelves; standing, walking, carrying, grasping, hearing, seeing, sitting, kneeling, climbing, balancing, stooping, crouching, and reaching. Working Conditions Work performed in a general office environment. Must be able to multi-task, meet deadlines, and work in a fast-paced environment. May require availability for overtime hours during peak periods. Share job details to About Life University Shape the future of health sciences and holistic education. Be part of a mission-driven team that values innovation and integrity. Apply today! Located in Marietta, GA, our 110-acre campus offers a collaborative environment for faculty and staff to innovate, educate, and serve. www.life.edu Join a team that empowers leaders to act with integrity and make a lasting impact on communities worldwide. Our Mission Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/39C3B08FA765F09BC547D09C6AC939C8/jobs/81396": {
      "title": "Paraprofessional II - Finance & Acquisitions (4388)",
      "description": "Paraprofessional II - Finance & Acquisitions (4388) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Paraprofessional II - Finance & Acquisitions (4388) Main Campus - Marietta, GA 30060 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Staff Apply Description The purpose of the Acquisitions Paraprofessional is to manage all library purchases including library information resources, maintain library budget information, collect and maintain accurate library financial records and statistics, and provide general library business clerical support.  This position works collaboratively with library cataloging staff. ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS Receives requests for library materials and performs pre-order research and verification of bibliographic data in electronic resources such as local on-line catalog, OCLC, and the Internet; identifies vendors and locates university vendor codes in EagleNet, as well as confirming availability of materials. Enters orders in the library’s on-line catalog and acquisition system.  Identifies funds for payment and notifies supervisor of funds status. Monitors open orders.  Communicates with university faculty and staff and external vendors to clarify status of requests, orders, and payments. Receives materials, updates on-line file and enters invoices in on-line system.  Sorts and distributes materials for cataloging and processing. Matches invoices to payment vouchers, exports invoice data to EagleNet according to established procedures and sends invoices to Accounts Payable for payment. Confirms that invoices were paid properly in EagleNet; confirms receipt of material for advance payments to vendors and confirms receipt of materials for prepayments to specialized distributors. Resolves problems and answers questions from requesters, vendors, and other library staff.  Returns incorrect materials, tracks payments, and maintains appropriate support files such as vendor catalogs, correspondence and addresses. Enters rush orders on demand, verifies status of orders and invoices.  Merges duplicate records for coworkers. Advises collection development staff, librarians, and faculty about availability of new materials.  Sorts and distributes publishers’ and vendors’ catalogs and notices. Monitors and maintains Library budget information. Processes library cash deposits. Monitors and maintains Library office supplies. Records and maintains accurate statistics on area activities and produces relevant reports. Additional duties and responsibilities as assigned. ADDITIONAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Assist with special projects and initiatives as needed or directed. Exhibits student centeredness in the performance of all job duties. Treats others with respect; understands the impact of culture/background on the behavior of others; respects differences among the Life community and demonstrates inclusive behavior. Anticipates, listens to, understands, and responds to customer needs.  Delivers work products and services to customers in a way that reflects positively upon the department and the University. Modifies shifts as needed during quarterly extended hours and breaks. Qualifications A vocational technical or A.S. degree with knowledge of budgeting and finance is required.  Several years of equivalent experience in a library setting may be considered. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS A B.S. Degree in Business Administration or the equivalent with experience with library services and technology is desired. KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, ABILITIES, AND PERSONAL CHARACTERISTICS Able to perform duties independently with general supervision. Basic math skills (addition, subtraction, multiplication, and division). Knowledge of basic accounting practices and skills. Computer skills; data entry and spreadsheet software capabilities. Strong attention to detail; ability to organize work and perform duties with a high level of accuracy. Strong interpersonal skills; including oral and written communication skills, listening skills, team building, and presentation skills. Demonstrate integrity and professionalism in appearance and demeanor. Ability to share and impart knowledge and reasoning to others especially during controversial encounters. Ability to develop and manage budgets. PHYSICAL DEMANDS Nature of work requires an ability to operate standard business office equipment and competency and proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite. Requires ability to communicate and exchange information, collect, compile, and prepares work documents, set-up and maintain work files. Must be able to lift up to 25 lbs.  Shelving library materials on high and low shelves, managing boxes of materials, kneeling, stooping, reaching, and transporting book carts with library resources is required. WORKING CONDITIONS Work performed in a general office environment. May require availability for overtime hours as required. Share job details to About Life University Shape the future of health sciences and holistic education. Be part of a mission-driven team that values innovation and integrity. Apply today! Located in Marietta, GA, our 110-acre campus offers a collaborative environment for faculty and staff to innovate, educate, and serve. www.life.edu Join a team that empowers leaders to act with integrity and make a lasting impact on communities worldwide. Our Mission Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/39C3B08FA765F09BC547D09C6AC939C8/jobs/80909": {
      "title": "Advancement Services Manager (4352)",
      "description": "Advancement Services Manager (4352) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Advancement Services Manager (4352) Main Campus - Marietta, GA 30060 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Staff Apply Description The Advancement Services Manager position serves as the lead staff member responsible for managing gift processing, donor acknowledgments, and various financial reports, and maintaining and enhancing stewardship programs. The Advancement Services Manager has significant responsibilities for data and gift entry to ensure all cash gifts, stock donations, and pledges are accurately recorded in the Raiser’s Edge database and reconciled with the Financial Office. This position also provides administrative support and assistance to the University Advancement department by answering and directing phone calls, assisting with data entry, and performing other duties as requested. Job Responsibilities: Handle all duties related to processing recording and acknowledging gifts in the Raiser’s Edge. Manage and prioritize day-to-day gift processing activities and ensure accurate processing of checks, credit cards, and electronic funds transfers for unrestricted and restricted gifts and stewardship of gifts. Responsible for the optimization of all Advancement gift processing as well as ensuring that all processing is compliant with internal and external data privacy and gift recording policies, procedures, and regulations, including institutional, association, state, federal and international regulations and laws. Process data sets from Blackbaud Net Community (BBNC) and other external software solutions (Cvent, etc.) which include online donations, participant set up, profile updates and event registrations. Handle highly sensitive information and maintain strict confidentiality on all materials. Adhere to established University and departmental data integrity standards. Reconcile batches with Raiser’s Edge and prepare batches for daily deposit. Produce and distribute accurate tax receipts to donors for tax deduction purposes, ensuring accuracy and compliance with IRS guidelines. Generate and issue gift acknowledgement letters and tribute notifications for every gift within a designated benchmarked timeframe for Institutional Advancement and the Office of the President. Maintain accurate records of all gifts and receipts for audit purposes and maintain appropriate internal documentation for the University. Manage quarterly or as needed updates of acknowledgement letter templates including drafting new copy. Interact professionally with Life University donors to give gratitude while securing confidential gift information. Communicate with Director of Advancement Services to ensure accurate processing of gifts and to ensure financial integrity and accuracy. Communicate with the Database Administrator and Finance Department to resolve technical problems or adjustments that must be made to ensure accurate processing of gifts. Work with Director of Advancement Services and Database Administrator to develop and maintain procedures manual for usage of Raiser’s Edge as it relates to the Advancement Division. Serve as a point of expertise on gift processing matters including excellent knowledge of IRS and other gift reporting, recording and acknowledgment rules, regulations and processes. Manage bi-weekly employee payroll deductions with Payroll Supervisor, reconcile batches for posting. Process special handling of non-routine deposits. Record donor pledges in Raiser’s Edge and maintain all pledge files. Track outstanding pledges and produce pledge reminder letters to donors and reports as appropriate. Adjust gifts and pledges as directed by the VP or Director of Advancement Services. Implement and manage donor stewardship programs. Identify best practices at other organizations for stewardship planning and operation. Work with the Advancement Division to develop and implement stewardship strategies that strengthen long-term relationships with donors at various recognition levels. Ensure that details of stewardship plans are compiled and communicated to all involved parties, and that the plan is documented, implemented and included in the moves management system. Develop and maintain stewardship efforts in Raiser’s Edge; track information, monitor activity and produce reports. Coordinate stewardship information listed in University-wide publications and on the website. Log prospect and donor news, communication, and information into Raiser’s Edge records. Verify and update biographical data in Raiser’s Edge as provided by Development Officers, and constituent information on checks and/or correspondence to ensure the accuracy of the database. Assist with database projects as needed. Event management including but not limited to event setup and breakdown, management of attendee and donor check-in process, donation processing as needed. Provide all aspects of administrative support for departmental operations, including but not limited to answering phone calls and providing information about the programs within the department. Additional Duties And Responsibilities Assumes additional responsibilities and performs special projects as needed or directed. Exhibits student centeredness in performance of all job duties. Treats all others with respect; understands the impact of culture/background on the behavior of others; respects differences among the Life University community and demonstrates inclusive behavior. Anticipates, listens to, understands, and responds to customer needs. Delivers work products and services to customers in a way that reflects positively upon the department and the University. Qualifications Required Qualifications Education, Training and/or Experience A B.S. degree in Business Administration or the equivalent years of experience in Advancement Services is desired. Must have one (1) to three (3) years of experience in gift processing and strong Raiser’s Edge usage including queries, exports and reporting skills. Collaborative work style to support the Advancement needs for information. Physical Demands Long periods of time working at a computer terminal. Nature of work requires the ability to operate standard business office equipment. Requires ability to communicate and exchange information, collect, compile, compare, and prepare work documents, set-up and maintain work files. Must spend majority of time concentrating on gift entry and management, donor relations, identifying and updating information and performing data entry input. Must be able to lift up to 25 lbs; retrieving and placing materials on high shelves and on floor-level shelves; standing, walking; carrying; grasping; hearing; seeing; sitting; kneeling; climbing; balancing; stooping; crouching and reaching. Working Conditions Work performed in a general office environment. May require availability for overtime hours during peak periods. Share job details to About Life University Shape the future of health sciences and holistic education. Be part of a mission-driven team that values innovation and integrity. Apply today! Located in Marietta, GA, our 110-acre campus offers a collaborative environment for faculty and staff to innovate, educate, and serve. www.life.edu Join a team that empowers leaders to act with integrity and make a lasting impact on communities worldwide. Our Mission Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/39C3B08FA765F09BC547D09C6AC939C8/jobs/80573": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant I - COC (4335)",
      "description": "Administrative Assistant I - COC (4335) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Administrative Assistant I - COC (4335) Main Campus - Marietta, GA 30060 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Staff Education Level High School Category Admin - Clerical Apply Description JOB PURPOSE The Administrative Assistant provides comprehensive administrative and operational support to the College of Chiropractic. This position supports the Dean’s Office, faculty, administrators, students, and visitors by coordinating schedules, preparing correspondence and documents, maintaining records, responding to inquiries, and supporting the school’s daily academic and administrative activities. The Administrative Assistant serves as a primary point of contact for the school and is expected to provide courteous, responsive, and professional customer service. The position requires strong organizational skills, attention to detail, discretion, and the ability to manage multiple responsibilities in a fast-paced academic environment. ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS Administrative Support Provide general administrative support to the Dean, school administrators, faculty, and other designated personnel. Manage calendars, schedule appointments, coordinate meetings, and assist with meeting preparation. Prepare agendas, reports, presentations, correspondence, spreadsheets, and other documents. Record and distribute meeting minutes when requested. Draft, proofread, format, and distribute routine communications. Receive, sort, and distribute departmental mail and electronic correspondence. Maintain organized electronic and paper files in accordance with University recordkeeping requirements. Order and maintain office supplies and assist with monitoring departmental inventory. Submit and track routine administrative requests, forms, invoices, purchase requests, and reimbursements. Assist with special projects and other administrative assignments as needed. Scheduling and Academic Support Assist with preparing and maintaining academic, faculty, meeting, and departmental schedules. Coordinate room reservations and schedule changes with the appropriate University departments. Communicate approved schedule information and changes to faculty, administrators, students, and other stakeholders. Assist faculty and administrators with preparing materials for meetings, classes, orientations, accreditation activities, and school events. Support the collection, organization, and maintenance of course, faculty, and departmental information. Track deadlines and provide reminders regarding required documents, meetings, reports, and school activities. Assist with faculty onboarding, orientation, and access to appropriate school and University resources. Help coordinate faculty meetings, professional development activities, student events, and other College of Chiropractic programs. ADDITIONAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Customer Service and Communication Serve as a welcoming and professional first point of contact for the College of Chiropractic. Respond to telephone calls, emails, visitors, and routine requests in a timely and courteous manner. Provide general information regarding school operations, schedules, procedures, and available resources. Direct students, faculty, employees, and visitors to the appropriate individual, office, or University resource. Exercise sound judgment when responding to questions and appropriately escalate sensitive, urgent, or complex matters. Build effective working relationships with faculty, staff, students, and other University departments. Maintain professionalism and composure when addressing competing priorities or difficult customer-service situations. Records and Information Management Maintain accurate faculty, departmental, scheduling, meeting, and operational records. Enter, update, and retrieve information from University systems and databases. Assist with compiling information and preparing routine reports. Monitor the completeness and accuracy of documents before submission or distribution. Handle confidential and sensitive information with appropriate discretion. Follow applicable University policies and requirements concerning student, faculty, employee, and institutional information. Operational Support Assist with coordinating school meetings, events, orientations, and other activities. Reserve meeting spaces and coordinate basic logistical needs, including technology, materials, attendance lists, and refreshments when applicable. Support departmental purchasing and expense-processing activities. Work collaboratively with Academic Affairs, Registrar, Human Resources, Information Technology, Facilities, Events, and other University departments. Identify routine administrative issues and recommend practical solutions or process improvements. Perform other duties consistent with the purpose and responsibilities of the position. PERFORMANCE EXPECTATIONS Successful performance in this position includes: Accurate and timely completion of administrative assignments. Reliable management of schedules, documents, records, and deadlines. Professional and responsive service to faculty, students, administrators, and visitors. Effective communication and collaboration across University departments. Appropriate handling of confidential or sensitive information. Consistent follow-through, dependability, and attention to detail. Positive support of the College of Chiropractic and Life University’s mission. Qualifications KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES Strong organizational and time-management skills. Advanced attention to detail and commitment to accuracy. Proficiency in preparing professional correspondence, reports, spreadsheets, presentations, and meeting materials. Ability to learn and use University systems, policies, and procedures. Ability to organize schedules involving multiple individuals, locations, and competing priorities. Ability to anticipate administrative needs and follow through on assignments. Ability to communicate effectively with individuals from different roles, departments, and backgrounds. Ability to remain professional, flexible, and solutions-oriented during periods of change or high activity. Ability to identify matters requiring immediate attention and appropriately involve the responsible administrator. Commitment to supporting the mission, values, and educational environment of Life University. REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS High school diploma or equivalent. At least three years of administrative support, office coordination, customer service, or related experience. Strong proficiency with Microsoft Office applications, including Outlook, Word, Excel, PowerPoint, and Teams. Experience managing calendars, scheduling meetings, preparing documents, and maintaining records. Strong written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Demonstrated ability to provide professional and responsive customer service. Ability to manage multiple assignments, establish priorities, meet deadlines, and maintain attention to detail. Ability to handle sensitive and confidential information appropriately. Ability to work independently while contributing effectively within a team environment. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Associate degree or higher. Administrative experience in higher education, healthcare education, an academic department, or a professional school. Experience supporting faculty, academic leaders, or senior administrators. Experience with academic scheduling, student information systems, document-management systems, or enterprise administrative systems. Experience coordinating meetings, orientations, or departmental events. Share job details to About Life University Shape the future of health sciences and holistic education. Be part of a mission-driven team that values innovation and integrity. Apply today! Located in Marietta, GA, our 110-acre campus offers a collaborative environment for faculty and staff to innovate, educate, and serve. www.life.edu Join a team that empowers leaders to act with integrity and make a lasting impact on communities worldwide. Our Mission Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/39C3B08FA765F09BC547D09C6AC939C8/jobs/79756": {
      "title": "Police Officer (4275)",
      "description": "Police Officer (4275) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Police Officer (4275) Main Campus - Marietta, GA 30060 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Staff Apply Description PURPOSE Under general supervision, monitors and patrols District facilities, property, and surrounding areas for the purposes of performing law enforcement, emergency response, and crime prevention functions to provide a safe environment for students, staff, and the public. ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS Develops and implements a student-centered approach to community policing, focusing on student development and assistance. Patrols to detect and deter crime and to help when need Maintain effective liaison with local outside law enforcement agencies. (i.e., Marietta Police Department, Cobb County Sheriff's Office, GEMA, etc.) Ability to lead law enforcement efforts in response to critical incidents. Ability to manage third-party private security contracts. Prepares required reports. Checks the security of buildings. Investigates suspicious activities or persons. Investigates traffic accidents and criminal or non-criminal incidents. Makes arrests and issue citations to individuals who have committed a crime. Responds to emergency incidents. Provides security and traffic enforcement at special events. Respond to calls for maintenance issues and relay information as needed. Assist local jurisdictions as outline in the Georgia mutual aid act. Qualifications REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS Education, Training and/or Experience Build and maintain positive working relationships with the public using principles of good customer service Sufficient experience to understand the basic principles relevant to the major duties of the position. Good standing with GA P.O.S.T Ability to successfully pass department background investigation. Ability to successfully pass Human Resources background investigation. Valid Georgia driver’s license. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and Personal Characteristics Strong interpersonal skills, including the ability to promote vision, work ethic, and accountability in a team environment. Ability to model integrity, character and leadership for providing excellence in chiropractic to humanity. Ability to model optimal citizenship attributes in the Life community. Ability to maintain mental concentration for extended periods of time. Ability to perform multiple duties in addition to departmental responsibilities with competing pressures and distractions. Ability to manage time effectively. Ability to tolerate, implement and embrace change. Capability to analyze and effectively resolve relational conflicts in clinical and other situations under routine and crisis demands. Certifications, Licenses, registrations Must be Georgia P.O.S.T. certified Valid Georgia Driver’s License or eligible to obtain within 30 days of hire. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS AA or AS Degree in Criminal Justice from an accredited College/University and two (2) years of law enforcement experience. PHYSICAL DEMANDS Nature of work requires an ability to operate security vehicle, computer equipment, and radio. Requires ability to communicate and exchange information, collects, compiles, compares, and prepares work documents, set-up and maintain work files. Must be able to lift between 40 lbs individually and up to 100 lbs with assistance; retrieving and placing materials on high shelves and on floor-level shelves; standing, walking; carrying; grasping; hearing; seeing; sitting; kneeling; climbing; balancing; stooping; crouching and reaching. WORKING CONDITIONS Work is mostly performed in a general office environment. However, there are times that this individual will cover for other officers in the field or on another shift. Each officer must be certified in the use of police equipment such as a firearm, handcuffs, radio and baton. This department is available 24/7. This job description is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties or skills required for the job and is subject to review and change at any time, with or without notice, in accordance with the needs of Life University.  Since no job description can detail all the duties and responsibilities that may be required from time to time in the performance of a job, duties and responsibilities that may be inherent in a job, reasonably required for its performance, or required due to the changing nature of the job shall also be considered part of the jobholder’s responsibility. Share job details to About Life University Shape the future of health sciences and holistic education. Be part of a mission-driven team that values innovation and integrity. Apply today! Located in Marietta, GA, our 110-acre campus offers a collaborative environment for faculty and staff to innovate, educate, and serve. www.life.edu Join a team that empowers leaders to act with integrity and make a lasting impact on communities worldwide. Our Mission Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/39C3B08FA765F09BC547D09C6AC939C8/jobs/79749": {
      "title": "Campus Safety Officer (4276)",
      "description": "Campus Safety Officer (4276) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Campus Safety Officer (4276) Main Campus - Marietta, GA 30060 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Staff Apply Description PURPOSE Provides professional security services for the University campus by controlling access to all buildings; patrolling the grounds and facilities; providing written reports based on daily activities; and performing specific duties pertaining to the safety, security, peace and order, and public relations of the University campus community. ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS Follows daily requirements for building locking and unlocking procedures. Periodically inspects buildings and grounds during the shift to ensure there is no physical damage. Patrols parking lots regularly to ensure traffic flow is not disturbed. Writes parking tickets when necessary. Impounds unauthorized vehicles according to established procedures. Assists visitors, students, faculty, and employees with vehicle problems, directions, and information as requested. Participates in organized programs for training, crime prevention, and community relations. Writes reports as necessary according to department protocol and documents all incidents as required. Develops good working relationships with other campus departments, faculty, and students. Answers the telephone and relays information to the appropriate personnel. Performs all other duties as assigned to support the Life University mission. Locks and unlocks doors on campus and surrounding property. Maintains familiarity with and supports the mission of Life University and Campus Safety. ADDITIONAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Assumes additional responsibilities and performs special projects as needed or directed. Exhibits student-centeredness in the performance of all job duties. Treats all others with respect; understands the impact of culture and background on the behavior of others; respects differences among the Life community; and demonstrates inclusive behavior. Anticipates, listens to, understands, and responds to customer needs. Delivers work products and services to customers in a manner that reflects positively upon the department and the University. Handles incidents to help ensure the safety of police officers and other first responders. Monitors radio channels and provides immediate information and assistance to police and other first responders. Qualifications REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS Education, Training and/or Experience A High School Diploma (or equivalent) with some security or law enforcement experience. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and Personal Characteristics Possesses some knowledge of federal, state, and local laws and regulations. Able to perform duties independently under general supervision. Able to prioritize and manage multiple projects while adhering to strict timelines. Strong interpersonal skills with a focus on conflict resolution. Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to communicate effectively at all levels. Well-developed analytical and problem-solving abilities. Able to organize work, engage in a variety of tasks simultaneously, and consistently meet deadlines. Able to write reports and business correspondence. Computer skills, including proficiency with Microsoft Office applications. Ability to perform CPR and basic lifesaving activities. Ability to observe and define problems, establish facts, and draw valid conclusions. Certifications, Licenses, Registrations A valid Georgia Driver’s License is required. Share job details to About Life University Shape the future of health sciences and holistic education. Be part of a mission-driven team that values innovation and integrity. Apply today! Located in Marietta, GA, our 110-acre campus offers a collaborative environment for faculty and staff to innovate, educate, and serve. www.life.edu Join a team that empowers leaders to act with integrity and make a lasting impact on communities worldwide. Our Mission Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/39C3B08FA765F09BC547D09C6AC939C8/jobs/78551": {
      "title": "Senior Manager of Enrollment Events & Tours (4218)",
      "description": "Senior Manager of Enrollment Events & Tours (4218) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Senior Manager of Enrollment Events & Tours (4218) Main Campus - Marietta, GA 30060 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Staff Apply Description Senior Manager of Events and Tours – Enrollment Position Summary The Senior Manager of Events and Tours leads the strategy, planning, execution, and continuous improvement of enrollment-focused events and tours designed to engage prospective students and their families, strengthen the enrollment experience, and drive conversion. This role manages the Events and Tours team and serves as a strategic partner across Enrollment, Marketing, Admissions, Student Services, and campus leadership. The Senior Manager ensures that every event and tour reflects the institution’s brand, provides an exceptional experience for prospective students and guests, and contributes measurably to enrollment goals. The role serves all enrollment audiences , developing experiences that support prospective students throughout the enrollment journey—from initial awareness and inquiry through application, admission, deposit, and enrollment. Key Responsibilities Enrollment Event & Tour Strategy Develop and execute a comprehensive events and tours strategy aligned with institutional enrollment objectives. Lead the design and evolution of prospective student events, campus tours, open houses, admitted-student programs, yield events, virtual experiences, and other enrollment initiatives. Create experiences that effectively communicate the institution’s academic programs, student experience, campus community, and value proposition. Identify opportunities to use events and tours to increase engagement, application, yield, and enrollment outcomes. Establish annual calendars, priorities, goals, budgets, and operational plans for enrollment events and tours. Event & Tour Operations Oversee the end-to-end planning and execution of enrollment events and tours, including logistics, staffing, communications, programming, facilities, vendors, technology, and guest services. Develop standardized processes and best practices that ensure consistent execution across events and experiences. Partner with campus departments and stakeholders to coordinate speakers, presentations, student ambassadors, faculty participation, facilities, and other event components. Ensure events and tours are accessible, welcoming, inclusive, and responsive to the needs of diverse audiences. Anticipate operational challenges and develop contingency plans to ensure a seamless prospective-student experience. Enrollment & Conversion Partner closely with Enrollment leadership to connect events and tours to recruitment and conversion strategies. Develop event experiences and follow-up strategies that move prospective students through the enrollment funnel. Use enrollment data and audience insights to identify opportunities to improve engagement, attendance, application, yield, and enrollment outcomes. Collaborate with Admissions and Enrollment teams to ensure event and tour experiences complement recruitment communications and outreach. Establish and monitor key performance indicators to measure the effectiveness and return on investment of events and tours. Marketing, Communications & Experience Collaborate with Marketing and Communications to develop event positioning, messaging, invitations, registration experiences, and follow-up communications. Ensure event content and guest experiences consistently reinforce the institution’s brand and enrollment messaging. Develop strategies to increase event participation and engagement among prospective students, families, admitted students, and other enrollment audiences. Gather and incorporate feedback from guests, students, families, staff, and campus partners to continuously improve the experience. Budget & Vendor Management Develop and manage event and tour budgets, ensuring resources are strategically allocated to support enrollment priorities. Negotiate and manage relationships with external vendors, partners, and service providers. Monitor expenditures and maintain appropriate financial controls and reporting. Assessment & Continuous Improvement Establish dashboards, reports, and performance measures to evaluate event and tour effectiveness. Analyze attendance, engagement, conversion, and enrollment data to inform future strategies. Conduct post-event assessments and implement improvements based on data and stakeholder feedback. Stay current with emerging trends and best practices in enrollment events, campus visitation, student experience, and higher education recruitment. Qualifications Required Bachelor’s degree or equivalent combination of education and relevant experience. Significant experience in event management, enrollment, admissions, recruitment, higher education, hospitality, or a related field. Demonstrated experience leading and developing teams. Proven ability to manage complex events, programs, and multiple priorities simultaneously. Strong project management, organizational, communication, and interpersonal skills. Experience using data and performance metrics to evaluate programs and inform decisions. Demonstrated ability to collaborate effectively across departments and with diverse stakeholders. Preferred Master’s degree in higher education, enrollment management, marketing, communications, business, hospitality, or a related field. Experience working in higher education enrollment, admissions, recruitment, or student experience. Experience managing campus tours and prospective-student or admitted-student events. Experience developing event strategies specifically designed to support enrollment conversion. Familiarity with CRM, event registration, scheduling, and enrollment management technologies. Core Competencies Strategic enrollment leadership Event and experience design Team leadership and staff development Project and operational management Relationship building and cross-functional collaboration Data-informed decision-making Budget and resource management Customer and guest experience Problem-solving and adaptability Continuous improvement Success in This Role Success will be demonstrated through a strong, high-performing Events and Tours team; exceptional experiences for prospective students and families; efficient and scalable event operations; strong collaboration across Enrollment and campus partners; and measurable contributions to prospective-student engagement, conversion, yield, and overall enrollment goals . Share job details to About Life University Shape the future of health sciences and holistic education. Be part of a mission-driven team that values innovation and integrity. Apply today! Located in Marietta, GA, our 110-acre campus offers a collaborative environment for faculty and staff to innovate, educate, and serve. www.life.edu Join a team that empowers leaders to act with integrity and make a lasting impact on communities worldwide. Our Mission Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/39C3B08FA765F09BC547D09C6AC939C8/jobs/78655": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Public Health (4225)",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty, Public Health (4225) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct Faculty, Public Health (4225) Main Campus - Marietta, GA 30060 Apply Overview Position Type Adjunct Faculty Category Education Apply Description Adjunct Faculty, Public Health Essential Job Functions Life University seeks applicants for an Adjunct Faculty to serve in our new Bachelor of Science degree program in Public Health. Our public health program emphasizes wellness, prevention, service, and community engagement within a population health framework. Supporting the University’s mission and vision, the program will approach public health as the study and promotion of conditions that support human potential and reduce barriers to optimal health and well-being. We are seeking dynamic instructors who will bring a creative and student-centered approach to the classroom and online instruction. Once hired, Adjunct Faculty in public health will be invited to teach and develop courses as needed. Primarily responsible for the instruction, supervision, and evaluation of students in the classroom as well as course assessments for the department. Prepare a syllabus for each course taught using the college template. Teach class in a professional manner, teaching the material that is present in the syllabus and course outline. Start and end each class on time. Communicate your teaching and student office hours schedule for each quarter and be present virtually during student office hours. Appropriately maintain all necessary records for each course taught. Attend scheduled meetings and events as appropriate and as requested by Assistant Dean of Social Sciences. Cultivate in oneself and others a commitment to helpfulness, building relationships, collaborating to find the best solution, and serving students with care and integrity. Qualifications Education, Training and/or Experience A minimum of three years of teaching or related professional experience is required. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and Personal Characteristics Strong teaching, presentation, and facilitation skills. Commitment to empowering students as scholars and professionals. Exceptional writing skills and experience. Ability to work with and maintain confidential student information. Strong interpersonal skills. High degree of initiative and independent judgment. Well-developed analytical and problem-solving abilities. Strong multimedia and computer skills. Commitment to an ethic of care and service. Preferred Qualifications A doctoral degree in Public Health or a closely related field is preferred. Candidates with a master's degree in public health or a graduate degree in a related field with relevant coursework and/or professional experience will also be considered. Research experience in Public Health or a related field is preferred. Experience developing, designing, or implementing new courses is preferred. Working Conditions Work performed in a general academic environment. Courses are offered on ground and online. Share job details to About Life University Shape the future of health sciences and holistic education. Be part of a mission-driven team that values innovation and integrity. Apply today! Located in Marietta, GA, our 110-acre campus offers a collaborative environment for faculty and staff to innovate, educate, and serve. www.life.edu Join a team that empowers leaders to act with integrity and make a lasting impact on communities worldwide. Our Mission Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/39C3B08FA765F09BC547D09C6AC939C8/jobs/74047": {
      "title": "Groundskeeper (4020)",
      "description": "Groundskeeper (4020) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Groundskeeper (4020) Main Campus - Marietta, GA 30060 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Staff Category Facilities Apply Description Life University is looking for a dynamic and compassionate individuals to serve as Groundskeepers. Under direct supervision, this position supports the Facilities Management- Grounds Department by maintaining the landscape of university property which includes irrigation maintenance, mowing, trimming, pruning, tree removal, planting and trash removal. This position performs a variety of landscape maintenance tasks to preserve and maintain the University Campus. This position is also responsible for campus snow removal which ensures safe driving conditions during the winter months and event support which includes furniture and/or material moves in support of special projects or initiatives. Responsible for working as a team member in developing and maintaining grounds maintenance work for the University campus.  Life University has developed and implemented an Honor Code and Standards of Conduct, which serve as a set of expectations for the living and learning environment provided by the University. This is an open application, and we will review applicants as positions become available. We appreciate your patience and look forward to considering your application when we are ready to expand our team. Responsibilities Perform a wide variety of tasks related to the maintenance, and upkeep of university grounds and facilities. Use appropriate landscaping methods to care for, preserve and water plants; sod, seed and fertilize lawns; prepare beds and properly install appropriate plant material. Understand and apply correct procedure for fertilizer mixture and application to all plant material on campus. Properly prune trees and shrubs. Provide maintenance for annuals and perennials, and other plantings as needed. Properly mow, edge, and trim lawns with appropriate tools, operate equipment properly so as to avoid injury to self and others. Always maintain safe working conditions by using supplies and equipment properly and taking necessary precautions. Properly care for and service power operated equipment used for grounds keeping activities. Clean-up and maintain University grounds. Pick up litter from university property, remove rubbish; empty outdoor garbage cans; rake and/or blow grass clippings and leaves; set up and operate sprinklers; remove debris. Must be able to initiate and complete basic landscape duties on campus to include mowing, planting, trimming, blowing, fertilizing and trash removal but also, trenching, sodding and site irrigation. Assists with all Special Event setup and break down. Perform clean-up and maintenance of interior areas as required. Assists with campus office relocations along with ensuring the trash is removed daily. Initiates and repairs any irrigation issues as needed. Qualifications Requirements Do you have a High School Diploma or Equivalent? Or are you willing to obtain a High School Diploma or Equivalent through Life's Educational Attainment Program? Must have a valid Georgia Driver’s License, or out of state license with the ability to obtain a Georgia Driver’s License within 30 days is required.  Must also be insurable under Life University’s insurance carrier. Physical Demands The nature of work requires an ability to operate standard grounds-related equipment. Other physical requirements are pushing/pulling carts weighing up to 100 lbs.; retrieving and placing materials on high shelves and on floor-level shelves; standing, walking; carrying; grasping; hearing; seeing; sitting; kneeling; climbing; balancing; stooping; crouching and reaching. Requires ability to communicate and exchange information, collects, compiles, compares, and prepares work documents, set-up and maintain work files. Must be able to lift between 40 lbs. individually and up to 60 lbs. with assistance. Working Conditions Exposure to dust, pollen, noxious chemicals, fuel, lubricants, solvents, and poisonous plants and/or animals is possible. May require availability for overtime hours during special events. Must wear gloves, safety glasses, ear plugs, insect repellant, and other necessary protective wear. This position will commonly complete tasks in inclement conditions including heat, humidity, cold, and rain. Work performed in an outside working environment. Share job details to About Life University Shape the future of health sciences and holistic education. Be part of a mission-driven team that values innovation and integrity. Apply today! Located in Marietta, GA, our 110-acre campus offers a collaborative environment for faculty and staff to innovate, educate, and serve. www.life.edu Join a team that empowers leaders to act with integrity and make a lasting impact on communities worldwide. Our Mission Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/39C3B08FA765F09BC547D09C6AC939C8/jobs/73774": {
      "title": "Academic Advisor (4006)",
      "description": "Academic Advisor (4006) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Academic Advisor (4006) Main Campus - Marietta, GA 30060 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Staff Category Education Apply Description Under general direction, the Academic Advisor is responsible for implementing a relationship-based Academic Advising model that reflects best practices and optimal support for students. Promoting a holistic and unified approach to academic advisement and academic success is the primary priority for the Academic Advisor. Academic Advisors are responsible for outcomes-driven efforts in academic advising, including but not limited to retention, progression, and graduation. Academic Advisors also serve as mentors for Academic Advisors. Essential Job Functions Follows the University advising model/plan to meet the needs of undergraduate, graduate, and professional students in on-ground and online programs. Answer questions from new and returning students regarding courses, registration process, and general advisement. Maintain accurate and appropriate information regarding caseload, and term to term management of that case load. Maintain check-in communication with current caseload and update communication in CRMAdvise. Collaborate with staff of the Registrar's Office, Admissions, Student Engagement, New Student Orientation, and Academic Learning Center as needed to contribute to students' smooth integration and transition to graduation. Assist with and coordinate administrative holds on registration. Provide timely data and reports as requested and directed. Contact and schedule appointments for new students to be advised. Work on-call to assist students without appointment. Audit new student academic plans to ensure students are selecting the correct classes. Mentor new academic advisors. Aid staff in supporting student needs as necessary within the department. Additional duties and responsibilities as assigned. Additional Duties And Responsibilities Exhibits student centeredness in performance of all job duties. Treats all others with respect; understands the impact of culture/background on the behavior of others; respects differences among the Life community and demonstrates inclusive behavior. Anticipates, listens to, understands and responds to customer needs. Delivers work products and services to customers in a way that reflects positively upon the department and the University. Qualifications Education, Training and/or Experience Master's Degree in College Student Personnel, Counseling or related field. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and Personal Characteristics Excellent oral and written communication skills. Ability to effectively use computer programs software (Microsoft Office Suite), hardware and presentation programs. Ability to maintain a courteous and professional attitude in stressful situations. Ability to perform assigned duties with frequent interruptions and time pressures. Ability to analyze and resolve routine and crisis situations. Certifications, Licenses, registrations None. Preferred Qualifications 1 year experience in academic advising at the collegiate level. Experience working with unique student populations. Experience facilitating first-year and academic success courses at the college level. Working knowledge of Datatel Colleague platform. Bilingual. Physical Demands Nature of work requires an ability to operate standard business office equipment. Requires ability to communicate and exchange information, collect, compile and prepare work documents, set-up and maintain work files. Must be able to lift 25 lbs., retrieving and placing materials on high shelves and on floor-level shelves; standing, walking, carrying, grasping, hearing, seeing, sitting, kneeling, climbing, balancing, stooping, crouching, and reaching. Working Conditions Work performed in an office environment. Some travel may be required. May require availability for overtime hours during peak periods. Share job details to About Life University Shape the future of health sciences and holistic education. Be part of a mission-driven team that values innovation and integrity. Apply today! Located in Marietta, GA, our 110-acre campus offers a collaborative environment for faculty and staff to innovate, educate, and serve. www.life.edu Join a team that empowers leaders to act with integrity and make a lasting impact on communities worldwide. Our Mission Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/39C3B08FA765F09BC547D09C6AC939C8/jobs/73228": {
      "title": "Admissions Recruiter - Doctor of Chiropractic Program (3987)",
      "description": "Admissions Recruiter - Doctor of Chiropractic Program (3987) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Admissions Recruiter - Doctor of Chiropractic Program (3987) Main Campus - Marietta, GA 30060 Start Date   07/24/2026 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Staff Travel Percentage Road Warrior Apply Description About Us Since 1974, Life University has been a trailblazer in postsecondary education, seeking individuals eager to join our team dedicated to shaping the future of health and wellness education. Situated in Marietta, Georgia, our university’s campus provides a nurturing, yet dynamic environment for academic and personal growth. We are a specialized institution focused on vitalistic education in the fields of healthcare, business administration, and the social sciences, providing a range of undergraduate and graduate degrees alongside our flagship Doctor of Chiropractic program. As we continue our mission to empower students and pioneer innovative approaches to vitalistic education, we are actively seeking passionate professionals to join us in our commitment to excellence. Serving Lasting Purpose At Life University, our mission extends beyond education—we strive to embody a Lasting Purpose: To Give, To Do, To Love, To Serve—out of your own abundance. Life University’s guiding principle is to live an inner-directed life, recognizing that the willingness and desire to serve your community and your fellow human beings are just as important as academic pursuits. This philosophy drives our commitment to our students, staff, and the broader community, inspiring us to make meaningful contributions to the world through the transformative power of education and service. We believe that everyone has unique gifts, and as a member of the global community, it is our duty to share those gifts generously, living by the principle of giving, doing, loving, and serving out of abundance. Equal Employment Opportunity Life University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We provide consideration for employment to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, disability, or protected veteran status. JOB PURPOSE The Admissions Recruiter for the Doctor of Chiropractic Program is responsible for identifying, engaging, and guiding prospective students through the admissions process. This role focuses on building relationships with undergraduate institutions, pre-health advisors, and prospective students interested in pursuing a Doctor of Chiropractic degree. The recruiter represents the institution at events, provides program information, and supports enrollment growth through strategic outreach and personalized communication. ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS Student Recruitment & Outreach Develop and implement recruitment strategies to attract qualified applicants to the Doctor of Chiropractic (DC) program. Build relationships with undergraduate institutions, particularly pre-health, kinesiology, biology, and exercise science programs. Conduct on-campus and virtual presentations about the DC program, career pathways, and admissions requirements. Represent the institution at college fairs, graduate school fairs, professional conferences, and recruitment events. Travel to partner institutions and recruitment events as needed. Applicant Engagement Serve as the primary contact for prospective DC students from inquiry through enrollment. Conduct one-on-one advising sessions with prospective students to discuss program requirements, prerequisites, and career opportunities in chiropractic. Respond promptly to inquiries via phone, email, and virtual meetings. Maintain ongoing communication with prospective students to nurture interest and guide them through the application process. Manage a designated recruitment territory, generating monthly 50+ prospective student inquiries, converting 40% to applications, achieving 80% acceptance yield, and 50% enrollment conversion through targeted outreach and relationship building with colleges and universities. Admissions Support Assist applicants with application submission, documentation, and prerequisite verification. Collaborate with the admissions team to review applicant pipelines and ensure timely follow-up. Track recruitment metrics and maintain accurate records in the CRM system. Support interview days, campus tours, and admitted student events. ADDITIONAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Relationship Development Develop partnerships with pre-health advisors, faculty, and student organizations at feeder institutions. Build relationships with chiropractic clinics, professional associations, and community partners to promote the profession. Participate in professional networking events to increase program visibility. Data & Reporting Monitor recruitment performance and enrollment trends. Provide regular reports on recruitment activities, lead generation, and conversion rates. Use data insights to refine recruitment strategies and improve outcomes. Qualifications REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor’s degree in higher education, communications, business, health sciences, or a related field. 2+ years of experience in admissions, recruitment, sales, or student advising. Strong presentation and public speaking skills. Ability to travel frequently for recruitment events. Excellent interpersonal, communication, and relationship-building skills. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Experience recruiting for graduate or professional programs. Familiarity with healthcare education or chiropractic programs. Experience using CRM systems for lead management. Knowledge of the chiropractic profession and healthcare career pathways. KEY COMPETENCIES Relationship building and networking Public speaking and presentations Sales and enrollment strategy Student advising and mentorship Organization and time management Data-driven decision making WORK ENVIRONMENT Combination of office and travel-based work. Frequent travel to universities, recruitment fairs, and events. Occasional evening and weekend work may be required for recruitment activities. COMPENSATION & BENEFITS Competitive salary based on experience. Health, dental, and vision benefits. Retirement plan options. Professional development opportunities. Travel reimbursement. PHYSICAL DEMANDS Nature of work requires an ability to operate standard business office equipment. Requires ability to communicate and exchange information, collects, compiles, compares, and prepares work documents, set-up and maintain work files. Must spend majority of time concentrating on CRT identifying and updating information and performing data entry input. Must be able to lift up to 25 lbs; retrieving and placing materials on high shelves and on floor-level shelves; standing, walking; carrying; grasping; hearing; seeing; sitting; kneeling; climbing; balancing; stooping; crouching and reaching. Share job details to About Life University Shape the future of health sciences and holistic education. Be part of a mission-driven team that values innovation and integrity. Apply today! Located in Marietta, GA, our 110-acre campus offers a collaborative environment for faculty and staff to innovate, educate, and serve. www.life.edu Join a team that empowers leaders to act with integrity and make a lasting impact on communities worldwide. Our Mission Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/39C3B08FA765F09BC547D09C6AC939C8/jobs/73219": {
      "title": "PT Front Desk Associate (3988)",
      "description": "PT Front Desk Associate (3988) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account PT Front Desk Associate (3988) Main Campus - Marietta, GA 30060 Start Date   07/24/2026 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Staff Apply Description The Front Desk Associate provides a positive first point of contact for patients and visitors entering the clinic, ensuring smooth, efficient, and timely patient flow at all times. This position is responsible for creating and updating patient records, obtaining required signatures, providing clerical support and assistance, escorting patients throughout the clinic, and providing general information regarding the clinic system. In this capacity, the Front Desk Associate is familiar with and supports the mission of the University, College of Chiropractic, and Clinic System. Position Status: Part Time Job Responsibilities Provides accurate and helpful information regarding the clinics to all inquiries, in person or over the phone. Ensures accurate, timely, and knowledge-based responses are communicated and discussed with patients and potential patients relating to chiropractic care, University Clinics, and the University. Greets patients and visitors and ensures a successful and high-quality visit and patient experience. Responsible for keeping abreast and maintaining working knowledge of third-party payers and Medicare regulations. Verifies insurance benefits and provides information to patents regarding insurance, copays, deductibles, and balances due by patient. Provides high-quality customer service and ensures that patients are well cared for. Interacts pleasantly and professionally with student interns, clinicians, patients, and visitors. Escorts patients to exam rooms and participates in the patient chiropractic education program when requested. Schedules patients in person or over the phone. Maintains knowledge of all patient forms and prepares patient files and forms; enters patient data into computer system. Ensures all demographic information is correct in the electronic health record. Ensures all patients are checked-in and have completed all required patient forms. Ensure that all patient records are scanned into the system accurately and promptly. Maintains the accuracy, quality, and correct location of sign-in sheets, patient files in the EHR, and any other applicable patient visit records. Coordinates patient records with other departments of the clinic system ensuring compliance with HIPPA regulations and confidentiality. Assists with the preparation of clinic reports as requested. Assists with the preparation and sending of Medical Records. Maintains all office areas in a neat, clean, and orderly manner. Promptly reports any equipment that is not in working order. Monitors waiting room for cleanliness. Monitors waiting room to ensure timely patient visits. Assists with other duties as assigned. Additional Duties And Responsibilities Assumes additional responsibilities and performs special projects as needed or directed. Exhibits patient centeredness in performance of all job duties. Treats all others with respect; understands the impact of culture/background on the behavior of others; respects differences among the Life community and demonstrates inclusive behavior. Anticipates, listens to, understands, and responds to the needs of others. Delivers work products and services to customers in a way that reflects positively upon the clinic and the University. Qualifications Education, Training and/or Experience Associate’s degree, or combination of High School/Equivalency and five years’ previous experience. Two years’ experience in clinical chiropractic setting, a business office or other clinical environment may be considered. Demonstrated computer skills, including experience with Microsoft Office Suites. Experience with electronic health records software and procedures. Excellent customer service skills. Demonstrated ability to maintain focus and work autonomously. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor’s degree. Five years’ experience in clinical chiropractic setting. Experience with electronic health records using NextGen software. Experience with insurance. Proficient knowledge in Microsoft Office Suites. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and Personal Characteristics Able to perform duties independently with supervision generally available at all times. Able to perform basic math skills (addition, subtraction, multiplication, and division). Ability to deal with difficult situations involving sensitive and confidential issues. Interact patiently and compassionately with diverse populations. Patience and compassion towards patients and other stakeholders with a pleasant personality. Ability to operate standard office equipment and follow office procedures. Ability to deal with difficult situations involving sensitive and confidential issues. Must be able to perform assigned duties with frequent interruptions and time pressures. Ability to communicate with all levels with confidence and knowledge. Ability to work effectively with a broad range of constituents in a diverse community. Effective oral and written communication skills. Able to organize work, engage in a variety of tasks simultaneously and consistently meet deadlines. Strong attention to detail. Maintains neat, clean, professional appearance as directed by University policy. Be knowledgeable about and know the location of information resources:  Intern Handbooks, Clinic SOP Manual, Clinic Staff SOP Manual, Clinic Department handbooks. Physical Demands Nature of work requires an ability to operate standard business office equipment. Requires ability to communicate and exchange information, collects, compiles, compares, and prepares work documents, set-up and maintain work files. Must spend majority of time concentrating on CRT identifying and updating information and performing some data entry input. Must be able to lift up to 25 lbs.; retrieving and placing materials on high shelves and on floor-level shelves; standing, walking; carrying; grasping; hearing; seeing; sitting; kneeling; climbing; balancing; stooping; crouching and reaching. Working Conditions: Work performed in a general doctors’ or clinical environment. Share job details to About Life University Shape the future of health sciences and holistic education. Be part of a mission-driven team that values innovation and integrity. Apply today! Located in Marietta, GA, our 110-acre campus offers a collaborative environment for faculty and staff to innovate, educate, and serve. www.life.edu Join a team that empowers leaders to act with integrity and make a lasting impact on communities worldwide. Our Mission Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/39C3B08FA765F09BC547D09C6AC939C8/jobs/73044": {
      "title": "HVAC Preventative Maintenance Technician (3973)",
      "description": "HVAC Preventative Maintenance Technician (3973) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account HVAC Preventative Maintenance Technician (3973) Main Campus - Marietta, GA 30060 Start Date   07/23/2026 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Staff Apply Description Job Description: Under the direct supervision of the Physical Plant Director, responsible for the maintenance of all heating, ventilating and air conditioning equipment.  Performs day-to-day inspection of all HVAC equipment.  Responds to routine trouble calls from employees or Departments who are “hot” or “cold”.  Provides primary surveillance over the HVAC maintenance contractors. ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS Provide maintenance and operating plans and procedures to keep all HVAC equipment in peak operating condition. Constantly monitors equipment and operating conditions to assure occupant comfort, yet optimize energy conservation. Monitors critical HVAC equipment operating procedures for potential equipment downtime, due to malfunction.  Advises in areas requiring attention.  Is accountable for the water treatment program, as assigned. Keeps all HVAC equipment logs, maintenance schedules, and operating manuals and diagrams current. Performs hands-on routine maintenance and repairs as needed on HVAC equipment. Accompanies the HVAC service contractors on property as directed. Performs periodic routine inspections of equipment, mech. rooms, cleanups, corrosion control and the like. Monitors the energy management systems to assure controls and schedules are functioning properly at all times. Performs any emergency maintenance as required to assure building operation. Responds to HVAC maintenance requests, i.e. hot and cold calls and follows up to assure area temperatures are within operating guidelines. Monitors the HVAC spare-parts inventory and advises inventory control on spares needed. Participate in acceptance and turnover of new equipment. Assures that all warranties, operating manuals and diagrams are received and submitted to the office manager Advises Physical Plant Director on methods to fine tune operating and maintenance procedures to minimize operating costs, and maximize consistent operating temperatures. Performs other Non HVAC related repairs and maintenance as requested ADDITIONAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Assumes additional responsibilities and performs special projects as needed or directed. Exhibits student centeredness in performance of all job duties. Treats all others with respect; understands the impact of culture/background on the behavior of others; respects differences among the Life community and demonstrates inclusive behavior. Anticipates, listens to, understands and responds to customer needs.  Delivers work products and services to customers in a way that reflects positively upon the department and the University. Qualifications Education, Training and/or Experience High School Diploma or equivalent. Five (5) years demonstrated competency in air conditioning and refrigeration HVAC Certification EAP Universal certification Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and Personal Characteristics Able to perform duties independently with general supervision. Excellent oral and written communication skills. Certifications, Licenses, registrations HVAC Certification EAP Universal certification Preferred Qualifications Experience working within an educational institution or commercial building PHYSICAL DEMANDS Able to climb a ladder. Requires ability to communicate and exchange information, collects, compiles, compares, and prepares work documents, set-up and maintain work files. Must be able to lift up to 50 lbs; retrieving and placing materials on high shelves and on floor-level shelves; standing, walking; carrying; grasping; hearing; seeing; sitting; kneeling; climbing; balancing; stooping; crouching and reaching. WORKING CONDITIONS 50% of work performed will be outdoors, on the roofs of the buildings. May require availability for overtime hours during peak periods. Share job details to About Life University Shape the future of health sciences and holistic education. Be part of a mission-driven team that values innovation and integrity. Apply today! Located in Marietta, GA, our 110-acre campus offers a collaborative environment for faculty and staff to innovate, educate, and serve. www.life.edu Join a team that empowers leaders to act with integrity and make a lasting impact on communities worldwide. Our Mission Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
