    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/39C3B08FA765F09BC547D09C6AC939C8/jobs/63251": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Business (3529)",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty, Business (3529) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct Faculty, Business (3529) Main Campus - Marietta, GA 30060 Apply Overview Position Type Adjunct Faculty Apply Description Life University is looking for an experienced, highly committed individual to serve at our Marietta, Georgia campus as an Adjunct Faculty member in the business program.  The successful candidate will fulfill the educational mission of the department, the college and the university in cooperation with the other members of the department and others in the university community. In addition to teaching face-to-face classes in various day and evening times, the adjunct faculty member will follow the curriculum set by the department. The adjunct faculty is responsible for managing, responding to and resolving reports and allegations of violations, as well as assessing the effectiveness of the University’s conduct system.  Life University has developed and implemented an Honor Code and Standards of Conduct, which serve as a set of expectations for the living and learning environment provided by the University. Responsibilities Comply with the Life University Honor Code as well as all university and college policies, including those in the Faculty Handbook. Primarily responsible for the instruction, supervision and evaluation of students in the classroom and/or laboratory setting as well as course assessments for the department. Prepare a syllabus for each course taught using the college template and post it to the class on the Blackboard site after approval from the Program Coordinator. Utilize strategies to relate technology concepts from class in a meaningful way to a range of students, especially for non-business majors. Teach class in a professional manner, teaching the material that is present in the syllabus and course outline while complying with guidance from the Program Coordinator. Start and end each class on time. Post in a prominent place your teaching and student office hours schedule for each quarter.  (One student hour is required weekly per class in addition to class time). Be present during student office hours.  Office hours are for the primary purpose of communicating with students regarding the courses you are teaching. Appropriately maintain all necessary records for each course taught. Submit IT work order requests as needed to address repairs and maintain the computer lab in optimum condition. Request peers to assist you in proctoring exams in very large classes.  For large classes, every exam should have at least one proctor and the instructor present. Attend scheduled meetings and events as appropriate and as requested by supervisor or program coordinator. Cultivate in oneself and others an attitude of helpfulness, personal commitment to building relationships, managing to the best solution, and user friendly always. Requirements Minimum of a Masters of Business Administration (MBA) or a masters degree in a related discipline. Substantial industry experience and industry Certification(s) preferred. Significant experience teaching face-to-face technology courses at the college level. Availability for travel to the Marietta campus multiple days throughout the week, with preference given to those with daytime schedule availability. Strong teaching and laboratory skills for face-to-face classes. (This position is not primarily for online classes.) Effective verbal and written communication skills. Commitment to maintain confidentiality in regard to students/employee information. Able to prioritize and manage multiple projects, adhering to strict timelines. Strong interpersonal skills. High degree of initiative and independent judgment. Well-developed analytical and problem-solving abilities. Advanced multimedia and computer skills. Share job details to About Life University Shape the future of health sciences and holistic education. Be part of a mission-driven team that values innovation and integrity. Apply today! Located in Marietta, GA, our 110-acre campus offers a collaborative environment for faculty and staff to innovate, educate, and serve. www.life.edu Join a team that empowers leaders to act with integrity and make a lasting impact on communities worldwide. Our Mission Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/39C3B08FA765F09BC547D09C6AC939C8/jobs/62527": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - MBA Program (1822)",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - MBA Program (1822) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct Faculty - MBA Program (1822) Fully Remote   •   Main Campus - Marietta, GA 30060 Apply Overview Position Type Adjunct Faculty Apply Description Department: College of Graduate and Undergraduate Studies Location: Life University, Marietta, GA (Remote) Life University is excited to be launching our MBA program in Fall 2025. To support our program, we are looking for experienced Faculty Members who would like to serve as Adjunct Faculty and teach some of our MBA course offerings. Position Summary The purpose of an Adjunct MBA Faculty Member is to fulfill the educational mission of the department, the college, and Life University by providing high-quality instruction in graduate business courses. We are currently accepting applications from qualified instructors to join our dynamic MBA program, particularly in the following areas: Accounting for Managers (Financial & Managerial Accounting) Corporate Finance / Financial Management Marketing Management Operations Management Strategic Management / Business Strategy Managerial Economics / Microeconomics Business Statistics / Quantitative Methods Business Law and Corporate Governance Organizational Behavior Leadership and Ethics This general posting allows interested candidates to express their interest and be considered as openings arise in various courses. Job Responsibilities: Comply with Life University’s Honor Code and Faculty Handbook policies. Deliver engaging, academically rigorous content in assigned MBA courses. Maintain classroom professionalism and foster a supportive learning environment. Prepare and publish a course syllabus via Blackboard each quarter. Maintain appropriate office hours and availability for student interaction. Complete necessary documentation and grading promptly and accurately. Participate in curriculum and assessment activities as needed. Attend department meetings and contribute to university initiatives. Stay current in field through ongoing professional development. Complete service hours and committee participation as outlined in the Faculty Handbook. About Us Since 1974, Life University has been a trailblazer in post-secondary education, seeking individuals eager to join our team dedicated to shaping the future of health and wellness education. Situated in Marietta, Georgia, our university’s campus provides a nurturing, yet dynamic environment for academic and personal growth. We are a specialized institution focused on vitalistic education in the fields of healthcare, business administration, and the social sciences, providing a range of undergraduate and graduate degrees alongside our flagship Doctor of Chiropractic program. As we continue our mission to empower students and pioneer innovative approaches to vitalistic education, we are actively seeking passionate professionals to join us in our commitment to excellence. Service Lasting Purpose At Life University, our mission extends beyond education—we strive to embody a Lasting Purpose: To Give, To Do, To Love, To Serve—out of your own abundance. Life University’s guiding principle is to live an inner-directed life, recognizing that the willingness and desire to serve your community and your fellow human beings are just as important as academic pursuits. This philosophy drives our commitment to our students, staff, and the broader community, inspiring us to make meaningful contributions to the world through the transformative power of education and service. We believe that everyone has unique gifts, and as a member of the global community, it is our duty to share those gifts generously, living by the principle of giving, doing, loving, and serving out of abundance. Qualifications Required Qualifications: Master’s degree in Business, Management, Economics, Finance, Accounting, Marketing, or a closely related field. Teaching experience at the collegiate level (online or in-person). Strong computer, communication, and instructional skills. Preferred Qualifications Terminal degree (Ph.D., DBA, JD, etc.) in a business discipline. Professional certifications such as CPA, PMP, SHRM-CP/SCP, CFA, or CMA. Demonstrated experience in curriculum development or online instruction. Knowledge, Skills, and Personal Characteristics Strong facilitation and presentation skills. Commitment to student success and inclusive teaching practices. Ability to work independently while collaborating across departments. Proficiency with digital learning tools (Blackboard, Zoom, MS Office, etc.). If you are passionate about educating future business leaders and thrive in a mission-driven academic environment, we encourage you to apply! Share job details to About Life University Shape the future of health sciences and holistic education. Be part of a mission-driven team that values innovation and integrity. Apply today! Located in Marietta, GA, our 110-acre campus offers a collaborative environment for faculty and staff to innovate, educate, and serve. www.life.edu Join a team that empowers leaders to act with integrity and make a lasting impact on communities worldwide. Our Mission Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/39C3B08FA765F09BC547D09C6AC939C8/jobs/58108": {
      "title": "On-Call Reserve Campus Safety Representative (3275)",
      "description": "On-Call Reserve Campus Safety Representative (3275) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account On-Call Reserve Campus Safety Representative (3275) Main Campus - Marietta, GA 30060 Apply Overview Position Type Seasonal Apply Description Job Title: Reserve Police Officer Department: Campus Police Reports To: Chief of Campus Police (or Designee) FLSA Status: Non-Exempt / On-Call Employment Type: Part-Time / Reserve / On-Call Position Summary Life University is seeking qualified and experienced Reserve Police Officers to support the Campus Police Department by providing on-call law enforcement services and additional coverage during peak periods, special events, emergencies, or staffing shortages . Reserve Officers play an important role in helping maintain a safe, secure, and welcoming campus environment for students, faculty, staff, and visitors while supporting Life University’s mission of Lasting Purpose and Student Success . Reserve Police Officers are not regularly scheduled employees and serve in an on-call capacity , working assignments as needed and approved by the Chief of Campus Police or designee. Key Responsibilities Provide on-call law enforcement services to supplement regular campus police staffing. Respond to calls for service , emergencies, alarms, and incidents occurring on university property. Patrol campus buildings, parking areas, residence halls, and grounds to ensure safety and security. Enforce state laws, local ordinances, and Life University policies . Assist with crowd control, traffic direction, and safety monitoring during campus events and activities. Conduct preliminary investigations of incidents, accidents, or suspicious activity. Prepare and submit incident reports and documentation in accordance with departmental procedures. Provide assistance and guidance to students, faculty, staff, and visitors. Support full-time officers during emergency response situations . Maintain familiarity with campus geography, safety protocols, and departmental procedures . Participate in required training and departmental briefings . Additional Information The On-Call Reserve Campus Safety Representative position is intended to provide supplemental safety staffing and does not guarantee a set number of hours. Assignments will be scheduled based on campus safety needs and employee availability . Life University values individuals who demonstrate professionalism, integrity, and a commitment to fostering a safe campus community. Qualifications Minimum Qualifications High school diploma or GED required. Prior experience in security, law enforcement support, campus safety, military service, or related field preferred. Ability to pass a background check and other pre-employment screenings. Valid driver’s license with acceptable driving record. Ability to work flexible hours including evenings, weekends, holidays, and special events . Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Strong observational and situational awareness skills . Ability to communicate effectively with a diverse campus community . Ability to remain calm and respond appropriately in stressful or emergency situations . Basic report writing and documentation skills. Strong customer service orientation and commitment to campus community safety. Ability to work both independently and as part of a team . Work Environment Work is performed both indoors and outdoors throughout the university campus. Duties may require walking, standing, and patrolling campus for extended periods . Work may occur during evenings, weekends, holidays, and special campus events . This position is on-call and scheduled on an as-needed basis depending on departmental needs. Share job details to About Life University Shape the future of health sciences and holistic education. Be part of a mission-driven team that values innovation and integrity. Apply today! Located in Marietta, GA, our 110-acre campus offers a collaborative environment for faculty and staff to innovate, educate, and serve. www.life.edu Join a team that empowers leaders to act with integrity and make a lasting impact on communities worldwide. Our Mission Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/39C3B08FA765F09BC547D09C6AC939C8/jobs/58101": {
      "title": "Reserve Police Officer (3276)",
      "description": "Reserve Police Officer (3276) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Reserve Police Officer (3276) Main Campus - Marietta, GA 30060 Apply Overview Position Type Seasonal Apply Description Job Title: Reserve Police Officer Department: Campus Police Reports To: Chief of Campus Police (or Designee) FLSA Status: Non-Exempt / On-Call Employment Type: Part-Time / Reserve / On-Call Position Summary Life University is seeking qualified and experienced Reserve Police Officers to support the Campus Police Department by providing on-call law enforcement services and additional coverage during peak periods, special events, emergencies, or staffing shortages . Reserve Officers play an important role in helping maintain a safe, secure, and welcoming campus environment for students, faculty, staff, and visitors while supporting Life University’s mission of Lasting Purpose and Student Success . Reserve Police Officers are not regularly scheduled employees and serve in an on-call capacity , working assignments as needed and approved by the Chief of Campus Police or designee. Key Responsibilities Provide on-call law enforcement services to supplement regular campus police staffing. Respond to calls for service , emergencies, alarms, and incidents occurring on university property. Patrol campus buildings, parking areas, residence halls, and grounds to ensure safety and security. Enforce state laws, local ordinances, and Life University policies . Assist with crowd control, traffic direction, and safety monitoring during campus events and activities. Conduct preliminary investigations of incidents, accidents, or suspicious activity. Prepare and submit incident reports and documentation in accordance with departmental procedures. Provide assistance and guidance to students, faculty, staff, and visitors. Support full-time officers during emergency response situations . Maintain familiarity with campus geography, safety protocols, and departmental procedures . Participate in required training and departmental briefings . Additional Information The On-Call Reserve Campus Safety Representative position is intended to provide supplemental safety staffing and does not guarantee a set number of hours. Assignments will be scheduled based on campus safety needs and employee availability . Life University values individuals who demonstrate professionalism, integrity, and a commitment to fostering a safe campus community Qualifications Minimum Qualifications Must be P.O.S.T. certified in the State of Georgia or eligible for certification. High school diploma or GED required; associate or bachelor’s degree in criminal justice or related field preferred. Prior law enforcement experience strongly preferred. Ability to successfully pass a background investigation , including criminal history review. Valid Georgia driver’s license with acceptable driving record. Ability to meet the physical requirements of law enforcement duties . Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge of law enforcement procedures, safety practices, and applicable laws . Strong interpersonal and communication skills with the ability to interact effectively with a diverse campus community. Ability to remain calm and make sound decisions in high-pressure or emergency situations . Ability to prepare accurate and timely incident and investigative reports . Commitment to professionalism, integrity, and community-oriented policing . Work Environment Work is performed both indoors and outdoors across the university campus. Duties may require standing, walking, driving, and responding to emergencies . Assignments may include evenings, weekends, holidays, or special events . This position is on-call and scheduled on an as-needed basis to provide additional departmental coverage. Additional Information Reserve Police Officers serve as supplemental law enforcement personnel and are not guaranteed regular hours. Scheduling is determined by departmental needs and officer availability. Life University is committed to creating a safe campus community and encourages candidates who value service, integrity, and community engagement to apply. Share job details to About Life University Shape the future of health sciences and holistic education. Be part of a mission-driven team that values innovation and integrity. Apply today! Located in Marietta, GA, our 110-acre campus offers a collaborative environment for faculty and staff to innovate, educate, and serve. www.life.edu Join a team that empowers leaders to act with integrity and make a lasting impact on communities worldwide. Our Mission Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/39C3B08FA765F09BC547D09C6AC939C8/jobs/57415": {
      "title": "Financial Aid Counselor I (3244)",
      "description": "Financial Aid Counselor I (3244) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Financial Aid Counselor I (3244) Main Campus - Marietta, GA 30060 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Staff Apply Description Location: On-Campus at Life University – 1269 Barclay Circle, Marietta, GA 30060 About Us Since 1974, Life University has been a trailblazer in postsecondary education, seeking individuals eager to join our team dedicated to shaping the future of health and wellness education. Situated in Marietta, Georgia, our university’s campus provides a nurturing, yet dynamic environment for academic and personal growth. We are a specialized institution focused on vitalistic education in the fields of healthcare, business administration, and the social sciences, providing a range of undergraduate and graduate degrees alongside our flagship Doctor of Chiropractic program. As we continue our mission to empower students and pioneer innovative approaches to vitalistic education, we are actively seeking passionate professionals to join us in our commitment to excellence. Service Lasting Purpose At Life University, our mission extends beyond education—we strive to embody a Lasting Purpose: To Give, To Do, To Love, To Serve—out of your own abundance. Life University’s guiding principle is to live an inner-directed life, recognizing that the willingness and desire to serve your community and your fellow human beings are just as important as academic pursuits. This philosophy drives our commitment to our students, staff, and the broader community, inspiring us to make meaningful contributions to the world through the transformative power of education and service. We believe that everyone has unique gifts, and as a member of the global community, it is our duty to share those gifts generously, living by the principle of giving, doing, loving, and serving out of abundance. Equal Employment Opportunity Life University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We provide consideration for employment to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, disability, or protected veteran status. Financial Aid Counselor I - Job Description Life University is looking for a dynamic and progressive individual to serve as the Financial Aid Counselor I. This role performs general aspects of financial aid administration under the supervision of the Director of Financial Aid and more senior staff. This individual assists students/families with the application process, reviews eligibility, advises students on process and programs, provides input to the creation and implementation of policies and procedures, and assists with regular office activities. Responsibilities Provide direct financial aid services to current and prospective students including financial aid application review, packaging of financial aid awards and financial aid counseling. Facilitate student success by counseling students on related financial literacy topics such as personal budget management, loan repayment, and other guidance which may affect student academic performance and continued eligibility for assistance. Assist with overall management of financial aid programs including federal, state, and institutional grants, loans, work-study, and scholarships. Through an extensive list of daily, weekly, monthly, and quarterly reports, complete timely review of student records to confirm financial aid eligibility and revise financial aid awards, ensuring that all aid (loans, grants, scholarships, and work-study) is properly awarded within federal, state and institutional guidelines. Oversee completion of student information and documentation collection. Make independent adjustments to a student’s financial aid record within federal and state regulations and the use of professional judgment. Represent the Financial Aid Department at orientation, recruitment events, and department presentations. Work collaboratively with Student Advocates, Student Accounts, Registrar, Enrollment, and other University constituents. Maintain confidentiality of student records. Participate in professional training and development opportunities as provided and serve as a member of the SAP Appeal Committee, and other committees as needed. Participates in University activities and committees that support the mission and initiatives of the University. Assumes additional responsibilities and performs special projects as needed or directed. Handles confidential information with discretion and independent judgment. Exhibits student centeredness in performance of all job duties. Treats all others with respect; understands the impact of culture/background on the behavior of others; respects differences among the Life community and demonstrates inclusive behavior. Anticipates, listens to, understands, and responds to customer needs.  Delivers work products and services to customers in a way that reflects positively upon the department and the University. Qualifications Requirements Bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution of higher education; OR the combination of an Associate's degree from an accredited institution of higher education AND three years of related experience. Demonstrated track record of delivering superior customer service. Proficiency in Microsoft Office suite (Excel, Word, Outlook, Teams, etc.) and data management. Must be, and remain, in good standing with personal Title IV loans. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities, and Personal Characteristics Ability to manage multiple and ever-changing priorities under established time constraints and in a professional manner. Motivated, organized, detailed oriented, strong communicator with excellent interpersonal skills and willingness to assist as needed in functions that support the mission and initiative of the University. Demonstrated commitment to student success and quality customer service delivery working within a diverse environment and interacting with students, faculty, staff, and visitors from different backgrounds daily. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with other staff members, campus departments, outside agencies, and students/families. Team building and organizational skills. High degree of initiative and independent judgment with the ability to perform duties independently with minimal supervision. Well-developed analytical and problem-solving abilities and general accounting skills. Demonstrate integrity and professionalism in appearance and demeanor; ability to share and impart knowledge and reasoning to others. Excellent oral and written communication skills with a high comfort level with speaking before large groups is required, and an ability to effectively engage audiences through dynamic oral presentations is essential. Share job details to About Life University Shape the future of health sciences and holistic education. Be part of a mission-driven team that values innovation and integrity. Apply today! Located in Marietta, GA, our 110-acre campus offers a collaborative environment for faculty and staff to innovate, educate, and serve. www.life.edu Join a team that empowers leaders to act with integrity and make a lasting impact on communities worldwide. Our Mission Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/39C3B08FA765F09BC547D09C6AC939C8/jobs/56474": {
      "title": "Patient Support Associate (3189)",
      "description": "Patient Support Associate (3189) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Patient Support Associate (3189) Main Campus - Marietta, GA 30060 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Staff Category Health Care Apply Description JOB PURPOSE The Patient Support Associate provides patient-facing and administrative support within the University Clinic System (including Radiology, Functional Kinesiology, Check-In, and Check-Out) to ensure a smooth, efficient, and timely patient experience. This position serves as a primary point of contact for patients and visitors, performing check-in and check-out, scheduling, payment processing, EHR documentation, and coordinating equipment, and documentation. In this capacity, the Patient Support Associate is familiar with and supports the mission of the University, the College of Chiropractic, and the Clinic System. ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS Assure appropriate patient flow and adapt when necessary. Crosstrain and maintain proficiency at all front-facing and support stations within the clinic system (e.g., Radiology, Functional Kinesiology, Check-In, Check-Out) and complete all required trainings within established timeframes. Serve as a positive first point of contact, greeting and assisting patients and visitors to ensure a high-quality patient experience. Provide accurate, helpful information regarding the clinics to all inquiries in person and over the phone. Communicate knowledgeably with patients and potential patients regarding chiropractic care, University Clinics, and the University. Perform patient check-in and check-out, including collection of outstanding balances; accurately post payments, provide receipts, and reconcile individual daily receipts with batch postings and applicable system reports (e.g., NextGen). Create, prepare, and maintain patient files and forms; enter and update demographic and clinical data in the electronic health record (EHR). Maintain knowledge of all patient forms and ensure all required forms are completed, scanned, and filed accurately and promptly in accordance with established QA procedures. Coordinate patient records with other departments of the clinic system, ensuring HIPAA compliance and confidentiality. Schedule new and recurring patient appointments in person and over the phone according to established processes. Monitor and maintain the cleanliness, orderliness, and readiness of waiting areas, exam rooms, office areas, and workstations. Promptly report any equipment or systems that are not in proper working order. Assist with the preparation of clinic reports and other clerical or administrative tasks as requested. Interact pleasantly and professionally with student interns, clinicians, faculty, staff, patients, and visitors. Perform additional duties and responsibilities as assigned . ADDITIONAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Exhibit strong student- and patient-centeredness. Anticipate, listen to, understand, and respond to the needs of patients, students, and other stakeholders. Perform special projects. Be an active participant in a culture of positivity, collaboration, and teamwork within the clinic system. Deliver work products and services in a manner that reflects positively on the clinic and the University. Treat all others with respect; demonstrate cultural awareness, inclusivity, and professionalism with diverse populations. Qualifications REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS Associate’s degree, or a combination of High School/Equivalency. At least two (2) years of experience in a clinical setting and business office. Experience with Microsoft Office Suite. Experience with electronic health records (EHR) software. Excellent customer service skills. Demonstrated ability to maintain focus, exercise good judgment, take initiative, and work autonomously. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Five (5) years of experience in a clinical setting. Experience with electronic health records. Proficient knowledge of Microsoft Office Suite. PHYSICAL DEMANDS Ability to operate standard office equipment. Ability to communicate and exchange information; collect, compile, compare, and prepare work documents; set up and maintain work files. Majority of time spent interacting with students and patients and working at a computer monitor to identify and update information and perform data entry. Ability to lift up to 25 lbs., including retrieving and placing materials on high and floor-level shelves. Ability to perform activities including standing, walking, carrying, grasping, hearing, seeing, sitting, kneeling, climbing, balancing, stooping, crouching, and reaching. WORKING CONDITIONS Work is performed in a general clinical environment. Share job details to About Life University Shape the future of health sciences and holistic education. Be part of a mission-driven team that values innovation and integrity. Apply today! Located in Marietta, GA, our 110-acre campus offers a collaborative environment for faculty and staff to innovate, educate, and serve. www.life.edu Join a team that empowers leaders to act with integrity and make a lasting impact on communities worldwide. Our Mission Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/39C3B08FA765F09BC547D09C6AC939C8/jobs/34182": {
      "title": "Manager, Brand & Digital Marketing (2232)",
      "description": "Manager, Brand & Digital Marketing (2232) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Manager, Brand & Digital Marketing (2232) Main Campus - Marietta, GA 30060 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Staff Apply Description Manager, Brand & Digital Marketing Location: Life University, Main Campus - Marietta, GA Essential Job Functions Responsible for elevating the Life University brand, increasing visibility, driving enrollment demand, and supporting the Life U culture through comprehensive marketing initiatives involving digital media, website design, content development, email, video, and traditional marketing channels. Develop branded content to drive engagement and grow our reputation through the website, social media, and at campus and community events. Script, plan, and oversee production of video and digital media. Manage integrated digital and traditional marketing projects. Plan budget, targeting, messaging, media, and creative strategies and tactics. Execute paid media initiatives including brand awareness and lead-generation. Develop email communication plans to support conversion of student inquiries to enrollment. Develop copy, cadence, and logic for multi-step communications and implement in CRM system. Conduct A/B testing of ads, landing pages, emails, and other tactics. Implement data-driven solutions to continually improve campaign results. Recommend, plan and implement other marketing initiatives supporting brand, culture, and enrollment. Develop and present communications to gain buy-in for marketing ideas, share progress, and report results and recommendations. Oversee each step of complex initiatives, document progress, and keep all stakeholders informed throughout. Monitor email, marketing, and media performance. Identify trends and insights. Implement improvements to optimize results. Support website development. Manage web initiatives from structure and design to page content, creative, and search engine optimization (SEO). Support SEO strategy utilizing BrightEdge or similar software. Conduct keyword research and apply results to advertising, website, and social media content. Conduct analysis and/or research to understand target audiences: demographics, psychographics, behaviors, preferences, and other insights to inform marketing strategy and content development. Manage external partners and/or specific initiatives: negotiate pricing, define detailed deliverables, and ensure expectations are met on time and within budget. Partnerships may include graphic designers, brand agency, media agency, video producers, photographers or others. Capture photo and video as needed to complement professional services and enhance marketing output. Design digital ads using Adobe, Canva, or similar software. Establish partnerships across campus with faculty, staff, leaders, and students to capture brand stories and effectively support strategic university initiatives. Collaborate with other departments to design strategies and tactics supporting university objectives. Ensure transparency and alignment on objectives and outcomes. Additional Duties and Responsibilities Serve as backup to team members as needed to support website edits or other project requests submitted to the marketing portal. May manage marketing personnel. Assumes additional responsibilities and supports special projects as requested. Qualifications Education, Training and/or Experience Bachelor’s degree in related field 3+ years of relevant experience Knowledge, Skills, Abilities Media strategy development Content strategy and creative development experience Presentation skills Data analytics and performance reporting Digital campaign management Microsoft Office Suite Software Email development system software Canva, Adobe Suite or similar design software Monday or similar project management software Google Analytics experience Salesforce, Ellucian, or other CRM software Budget management Cross-functional collaboration and partnership Partner/vendor management Personal Characteristics Collaborative Accountable Self-starter Works well independently Strong verbal and written communication skills Creative Innovative Flexible Analytical Customer service-oriented Student-centered Detail-oriented Results-oriented Values aligned with lasting purpose Preferred Qualifications Higher education marketing experience Wordpress or similar Content Management System (CMS) experience Photo/video experience Video editing skills Google certifications Hootsuite software Physical Demands Nature of work requires an ability to operate standard business office equipment. Requires ability to communicate and exchange information, collect, compile and prepare work documents, set-up and maintain work files. Must be able to lift 25 lbs., retrieving and placing materials on high shelves and on floor-level shelves; standing, walking, carrying, grasping, hearing, seeing, sitting, kneeling, climbing, balancing, stooping, crouching, and reaching. Working Conditions Work performed in an office environment. Some travel may be required. May require availability for overtime hours during peak periods. This position is in-person and requires residence in the Metro Atlanta area. Share job details to About Life University Shape the future of health sciences and holistic education. Be part of a mission-driven team that values innovation and integrity. Apply today! Located in Marietta, GA, our 110-acre campus offers a collaborative environment for faculty and staff to innovate, educate, and serve. www.life.edu Join a team that empowers leaders to act with integrity and make a lasting impact on communities worldwide. Our Mission Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/39C3B08FA765F09BC547D09C6AC939C8/jobs/8945": {
      "title": "Volunteer Assistant Coach (965)",
      "description": "Volunteer Assistant Coach (965) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Volunteer Assistant Coach (965) Main Campus - Marietta, GA 30060 Apply Overview Position Type Volunteer Apply Description The Volunteer Assistant Coach will assist the head coach with any aspects related to developing and maintaining a competitive program. Under the guidance of the Head coach, the volunteer will assist as directed to support phases of the program to include, but not limited to practice and competition support, skill instruction, record/statistic keeping, assisting in recruiting and any other related duties as assigned by the Head Coach. Responsibilities 1. Participate in meetings with the coaching staff, athletic trainers, and University staff to ensure coherent communication throughout the organization. 2. Assist with recruitment activities for student athletes. 3. Help with practice planning and implementation, as well as attend practices to help with coaching. 4. Assist department administrators in respective areas to ensure the student-athletes are meeting their responsibilities. 5. Assist with facilitating the code of conduct for student-athletes 6. Travel with team when necessary. 7. Assist with film breakdown when needed. 8. Assist in the efforts to promote the academic success of student-athletes. Qualifications 1. Ability to work without supervision and ability to speak clearly and use courtesy and tact in dealing with people. 2. Understanding of the rule requirements for the designated sport. 3. Able to work a flexible schedule throughout the year. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and Personal Characteristics 1. Strong Leadership Skills. 2. Team building skills – ability to work with coaches, vendors, and university officials effectively. 3. Strong oral & written communication skills. 4. Organizational focus. Preferred Qualifications Collegiate competitive experience in the described sport. Physical Demands 1. Ability to relocate equipment and supplies to various locations for athletic events. 2. Ability to drive to various locations. 3. Ability to lift and carry 40 pounds. Working Conditions 1. Work performed in various locations in and around the Life University campus, including athletic fields, track, and gymnasiums. 2. Some travel required. 3. Flexibility to accommodate schedules of athletic events. Share job details to About Life University Shape the future of health sciences and holistic education. Be part of a mission-driven team that values innovation and integrity. Apply today! Located in Marietta, GA, our 110-acre campus offers a collaborative environment for faculty and staff to innovate, educate, and serve. www.life.edu Join a team that empowers leaders to act with integrity and make a lasting impact on communities worldwide. Our Mission Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/39C3B08FA765F09BC547D09C6AC939C8/jobs/6375": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty (Open Application) (780)",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty (Open Application) (780) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct Faculty (Open Application) (780) Main Campus - Marietta, GA 30060 Apply Overview Position Type Adjunct Faculty Category Education Apply Description About This Opportunity: Life University is seeking to build a pool of qualified candidates as an open application for Adjunct Faculty positions in our College of Graduate and Undergraduate Studies, across various academic disciplines. While this is an open application, meaning specific positions in your area of expertise may not currently be available, your application will remain on file for consideration as needs arise within our programs. The purpose of faculty members is to fulfill the educational mission of the department, the college, and the university in cooperation with the other members of the department and others in the university community. Faculty positions are primarily in-person, aligning with the hands-on, collaborative nature of our educational approach. However, depending on the program and course offerings, opportunities to teach online sections may also be available. This flexibility allows us to serve a diverse range of student needs while providing faculty with an engaging and dynamic teaching environment. We welcome dedicated educators with a passion for teaching and a commitment to fostering student success. If you are interested in contributing to Life University’s mission as an Adjunct Faculty member, we encourage you to apply today. Job Responsibilities: Comply with the Life University Honor Code as well as all university and college policies, including those in the Faculty Handbook. Primarily responsible for the instruction, supervision, and evaluation of students in the classroom and/or laboratory setting as well as course assessments for the department. Prepare a syllabus for each course taught using the college template and post it to the class on the Blackboard site. Teach class in a professional manner, covering the material outlined in the syllabus and course outline. Start and end each class on time. Post in a prominent place your teaching and student office hours schedule for each quarter. Be present during student office hours, which are primarily for communicating with students regarding the courses you are teaching and for academic advising. Appropriately maintain all necessary records for each course taught. Request peers to assist you in proctoring exams. For large classes, every exam should have at least one proctor and the instructor present. Attend scheduled meetings and events as appropriate and as requested by your supervisor. Cultivate in yourself and others an attitude of helpfulness, personal commitment to building relationships, managing to the best solution, and a user-friendly approach at all times. Qualifications Education, Experience, and/or Training: Master’s degree in a relevant field is required; doctorate degree is preferred. Demonstrated teaching experience is required. Positions are primarily in-person; however, depending on the program, online sections may be available. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities, and Personal Characteristics: Strong teaching and laboratory skills. Effective written and verbal communication skills. Ability to work with and maintain confidentiality regarding student and employee information. Capable of prioritizing and managing multiple projects while adhering to strict timelines. Strong interpersonal skills. High degree of initiative and independent judgment. Well-developed analytical and problem-solving abilities. Proficiency in multimedia and computer skills. Share job details to About Life University Shape the future of health sciences and holistic education. Be part of a mission-driven team that values innovation and integrity. Apply today! Located in Marietta, GA, our 110-acre campus offers a collaborative environment for faculty and staff to innovate, educate, and serve. www.life.edu Join a team that empowers leaders to act with integrity and make a lasting impact on communities worldwide. Our Mission Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/39C3B08FA765F09BC547D09C6AC939C8/jobs/4273": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Chiropractic Science (618)",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Chiropractic Science (618) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct Faculty - Chiropractic Science (618) Main Campus - Marietta, GA 30060 Apply Overview Position Type Adjunct Faculty Apply Description Purpose The purpose of faculty is to fulfill the educational mission of the department, the college, and the university in cooperation with the other members of the department and others in the university community.  Faculty are responsible for didactic instruction of students in classrooms, laboratories, seminars, and other settings, as well as for professional practice instruction in clinics and other practice sites. Essential Job Functions Compliance with the Life University Honor Code as well as all University and college policies, including those in the Employee Handbook and the Faculty Handbook. Responsible for the instruction, supervision, evaluation and mentoring of students in and outside of the classroom and/or laboratory setting. On-going assessment of success in achieving learning goals of courses. Demonstrate assessment of success in achieving learning outcomes of course and program curricula. Maintenance of required academic records. Prepare a syllabus for each course taught according to the approved college template and post it to the respective Blackboard course. Remain current in the field of expertise Teach class in a professional manner, teaching the material that is present in the syllabus and course outline. Required to maintain and be available for student office hours for the primary purpose of communicating with students regarding assigned courses, mentoring and providing supplemental instruction, as required by the individual College. Attend faculty and departmental meetings, faculty development programs, or other meetings/events as required. Complete training as required by the individual College. Cultivate in oneself and others an attitude of helpfulness, personal commitment to building relationships, managing to the best solution, and user friendly always. Qualifications Required Qualifications And Experience Terminal Degree (where applicable) or degrees including areas of expertise: Certification(s) as applicable. Experience in university level instruction. Experience in other areas,( e.g., clinical, curriculum development, management) Experience teaching in on-line environment, where applicable. Preferred Qualifications 5 years’ experience in university level instruction. Experience with curriculum assessment and program review. Experience in multiple modalities of curriculum development and delivery. Share job details to About Life University Shape the future of health sciences and holistic education. Be part of a mission-driven team that values innovation and integrity. Apply today! Located in Marietta, GA, our 110-acre campus offers a collaborative environment for faculty and staff to innovate, educate, and serve. www.life.edu Join a team that empowers leaders to act with integrity and make a lasting impact on communities worldwide. Our Mission Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/39C3B08FA765F09BC547D09C6AC939C8/jobs/82315": {
      "title": "Registrar Credentialing Specialist (4450)",
      "description": "Registrar Credentialing Specialist (4450) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Registrar Credentialing Specialist (4450) Main Campus - Marietta, GA 30060 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Staff Apply Description LIFE UNIVERSITY About Us Since 1974, Life University has been a trailblazer in postsecondary education, seeking individuals eager to join our team dedicated to shaping the future of health and wellness education. Situated in Marietta, Georgia, our university's campus provides a nurturing yet dynamic environment for academic and personal growth. We are a specialized institution focused on vitalistic education in the fields of healthcare, business administration, and the social sciences, providing a range of undergraduate and graduate degrees alongside our flagship Doctor of Chiropractic program. Serving Lasting Purpose At Life University, our mission extends beyond education. We strive to embody a Lasting Purpose: To Give, To Do, To Love, To Serve - out of your own abundance. This philosophy drives our commitment to students, employees, and the broader community through education, service, and leadership. Equal Employment Opportunity Life University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We provide consideration for employment to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, disability, or protected veteran status. JOB PURPOSE The Registrar Credentialing Specialist supports the integrity, accuracy, and compliance of student academic records through the administration of enrollment verification services, transcript processing, credentialing activities, graduation operations, and student record management. This position serves as a primary resource for students, alumni, faculty, licensing boards, employers, and external agencies requiring academic verification and credentialing services. The Registrar Credentialing Specialist collaborates across university departments to ensure timely, accurate, and FERPA-compliant records administration while supporting graduation and commencement processes and delivering exceptional customer service. ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS Enrollment Verification Services & Credentialing Process enrollment and degree verification requests for students, graduates, employers, agencies, licensing organizations, and other authorized entities. Administer Parchment transcript services and oversee transcript order processing, fulfillment, and issue resolution. Coordinate student record requests and supporting documentation, including Apostille certifications, Great Sea requests, and other credentialing-related services. Complete athletic eligibility verifications and supporting certifications. Prepare and submit required CHECS reporting and maintain reporting accuracy and compliance. Complete state licensing board forms and documentation, including DC Student-at-Large requirements. Manage National Student Clearinghouse (NSC) enrollment and degree verification reporting, inquiries, and communications. Maintain accurate records and ensure compliance with institutional policies, FERPA regulations, and applicable reporting requirements. Graduation Operations Process graduation applications and conduct degree audits to verify fulfillment of academic program requirements. Coordinate degree posting, degree conferral, and graduation clearance activities. Manage initial and replacement diploma orders and graduation certificate preparation. Coordinate graduation-related communications with students, faculty, and university departments. Prepare and distribute academic honors designations, cords, and graduation-related materials. Generate graduation lists, commencement reports, and related institutional documentation. Develop and provide Registrar-related updates and content for commencement publications and graduation programs. Assist with commencement ceremonies, graduation events, and related activities. Registrar Office Operations Manage graduation processing queues and assigned workflow activities. Provide office coverage and serve as staff-on-duty as assigned. Assist students, alumni, faculty, and staff through walk-in support, telephone assistance, and electronic communications. Process incoming forms, records requests, and correspondence. Maintain electronic records, imaging systems, and document management workflows. Participate in departmental meetings, training initiatives, professional development opportunities, and cross-functional collaboration efforts. Support departmental projects, process improvement initiatives, and operational effectiveness efforts. Additional duties and responsibilities as assigned. ADDITIONAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Assist with special projects and university initiatives as requested. Support cross-training efforts within the Office of the Registrar to ensure operational continuity. Participate in ongoing process improvement and efficiency initiatives. Provide assistance during registration, commencement, and other peak operational periods. Attend university meetings, workshops, and professional development activities as appropriate. Qualifications REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS Education, Training, and/or Experience Associate's degree from an accredited institution of higher education in Business Administration, Higher Education Administration, Records Management, or a related field; bachelor's degree preferred. Minimum of two (2) years of administrative, records management, registrar services, student services, credentialing, or related professional experience. Experience working with confidential information and maintaining regulatory compliance. A combination of education and relevant experience may be considered in lieu of the stated educational requirements. Certifications, Licenses, Registrations None required. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor's degree in Higher Education Administration, Business Administration, or a related field. Experience working in a registrar's office, admissions office, academic records environment, or higher education setting. Experience with student information systems, electronic document management systems, and transcript service platforms. Experience processing National Student Clearinghouse reports and enrollment verifications. Experience conducting degree audits and supporting graduation administration. Knowledge of FERPA regulations and student records compliance requirements. PHYSICAL DEMANDS Nature of work requires the ability to operate standard business office equipment. Requires the ability to communicate effectively and exchange information with students, employees, alumni, licensing boards, and external agencies. Must be able to collect, compile, compare, review, and maintain electronic records and documentation. Requires extended periods of computer use and data entry. Must be able to occasionally lift up to 25 pounds. Requires sitting, standing, walking, bending, reaching, stooping, and carrying materials associated with normal office operations. WORKING CONDITIONS Work is performed in a professional office environment. Requires frequent interaction with students, alumni, faculty, staff, and external organizations. May require occasional evening or weekend work to support commencement ceremonies, graduation activities, or operational deadlines. May require overtime during peak registration, graduation, or reporting periods. Share job details to About Life University Shape the future of health sciences and holistic education. Be part of a mission-driven team that values innovation and integrity. Apply today! Located in Marietta, GA, our 110-acre campus offers a collaborative environment for faculty and staff to innovate, educate, and serve. www.life.edu Join a team that empowers leaders to act with integrity and make a lasting impact on communities worldwide. Our Mission Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/39C3B08FA765F09BC547D09C6AC939C8/jobs/82324": {
      "title": "PT Groundskeeper (4453)",
      "description": "PT Groundskeeper (4453) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account PT Groundskeeper (4453) Main Campus - Marietta, GA 30060 Apply Overview Position Type Part-Time Staff Apply Description Life University is looking for a dynamic and compassionate individuals to serve as Groundskeepers. Under direct supervision, this position supports the Facilities Management- Grounds Department by maintaining the landscape of university property which includes irrigation maintenance, mowing, trimming, pruning, tree removal, planting and trash removal. This position performs a variety of landscape maintenance tasks to preserve and maintain the University Campus. This position is also responsible for campus snow removal which ensures safe driving conditions during the winter months and event support which includes furniture and/or material moves in support of special projects or initiatives. Responsible for working as a team member in developing and maintaining grounds maintenance work for the University campus.  Life University has developed and implemented an Honor Code and Standards of Conduct, which serve as a set of expectations for the living and learning environment provided by the University. This is an open application, and we will review applicants as positions become available. We appreciate your patience and look forward to considering your application when we are ready to expand our team. Responsibilities Perform a wide variety of tasks related to the maintenance, and upkeep of university grounds and facilities. Use appropriate landscaping methods to care for, preserve and water plants; sod, seed and fertilize lawns; prepare beds and properly install appropriate plant material. Understand and apply correct procedure for fertilizer mixture and application to all plant material on campus. Properly prune trees and shrubs. Provide maintenance for annuals and perennials, and other plantings as needed. Properly mow, edge, and trim lawns with appropriate tools, operate equipment properly so as to avoid injury to self and others. Always maintain safe working conditions by using supplies and equipment properly and taking necessary precautions. Properly care for and service power operated equipment used for grounds keeping activities. Clean-up and maintain University grounds. Pick up litter from university property, remove rubbish; empty outdoor garbage cans; rake and/or blow grass clippings and leaves; set up and operate sprinklers; remove debris. Must be able to initiate and complete basic landscape duties on campus to include mowing, planting, trimming, blowing, fertilizing and trash removal but also, trenching, sodding and site irrigation. Assists with all Special Event setup and break down. Perform clean-up and maintenance of interior areas as required. Assists with campus office relocations along with ensuring the trash is removed daily. Initiates and repairs any irrigation issues as needed. Qualifications Requirements Do you have a High School Diploma or Equivalent? Or are you willing to obtain a High School Diploma or Equivalent through Life's Educational Attainment Program? Must have a valid Georgia Driver’s License, or out of state license with the ability to obtain a Georgia Driver’s License within 30 days is required.  Must also be insurable under Life University’s insurance carrier. Physical Demands The nature of work requires an ability to operate standard grounds-related equipment. Other physical requirements are pushing/pulling carts weighing up to 100 lbs.; retrieving and placing materials on high shelves and on floor-level shelves; standing, walking; carrying; grasping; hearing; seeing; sitting; kneeling; climbing; balancing; stooping; crouching and reaching. Requires ability to communicate and exchange information, collects, compiles, compares, and prepares work documents, set-up and maintain work files. Must be able to lift between 40 lbs. individually and up to 60 lbs. with assistance. Working Conditions Exposure to dust, pollen, noxious chemicals, fuel, lubricants, solvents, and poisonous plants and/or animals is possible. May require availability for overtime hours during special events. Must wear gloves, safety glasses, ear plugs, insect repellant, and other necessary protective wear. This position will commonly complete tasks in inclement conditions including heat, humidity, cold, and rain. Work performed in an outside working environment. Share job details to About Life University Shape the future of health sciences and holistic education. Be part of a mission-driven team that values innovation and integrity. Apply today! Located in Marietta, GA, our 110-acre campus offers a collaborative environment for faculty and staff to innovate, educate, and serve. www.life.edu Join a team that empowers leaders to act with integrity and make a lasting impact on communities worldwide. Our Mission Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/39C3B08FA765F09BC547D09C6AC939C8/jobs/82929": {
      "title": "Advancement Communications Manager (4491)",
      "description": "Advancement Communications Manager (4491) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Advancement Communications Manager (4491) Main Campus - Marietta, GA 30060 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Staff Apply Description The Advancement Communications Manager is a strategic member of Life University’s Office of Advancement, responsible for developing and executing the communications strategies to advance the department. This key member produces engaging, informative and compelling content that furthers Life University’s philanthropic priorities. The individual in this position will utilize several platforms, including print, web and email and should have working knowledge of best practices for each vehicle of communications. Serving as the communications leader for the Office of Advancement, this position develops compelling content, storytelling initiatives and multichannel communication strategies ((print, email, social media) that increase constituent engagement, promote philanthropic investment and elevate the visibility and impact of Advancement programs and initiatives. The Advancement Communications Manager collaborates closely with Development, Alumni & Friends, LIFEforce and University Marketing to ensure alignment with institutional priorities while maintaining Advancement's fundraising, stewardship and engagement objectives. Essential Job Functions COMMUNICATIONS Develops and implements a comprehensive Advancement communications strategy aligned with the University's fundraising, alumni engagement and institutional priorities. Creates annual communications plans, editorial calendars and messaging frameworks supporting Advancement initiatives, campaigns, events and engagement efforts. Serves as the primary communications strategist for the Office of Advancement and liaison with the Marketing Department. Works with members of the Office of Advancement division including the Vice President of University Advancement to identify, develop and implement a strategic communications plan for donors, alumni and friends and key stakeholders of the University that strengthens constituent engagement and philanthropic support. Responsible for segmentation, content creation and execution of email campaigns, newsletters and other Advancement communications targeting donors, prospective donors, alumni and friends of the University – through Raiser’s Edge NXT software. Responsible for buildout and formatting of any communications coming from the Office of Advancement to ensure brand standards align with Life University Marketing. Develops compelling donor-centric communications designed to elicit philanthropic support for Life University’s giving campaigns, including but not limited to annual giving, planned giving, and capital campaigns. Partners with other members of the Advancement Department to develop campaign communications, case statements, donor proposals, stewardship reports and impact communications. Partners with Alumni & Friends department to create communications that build lifelong engagement and strengthen relationships with Life University alumni and supporters. Develops communications including segmented newsletters that highlight alumni achievements, constituent success stories and institutional impact. Content to be provided by Alumni and Friends Department. Assists with writing and editing institutional messaging related to philanthropy on behalf of the Office of University Advancement. Provides editorial review and quality assurance for Advancement communications to ensure adherence to AP style, brand standards and institutional messaging. Develops and maintains Advancement-related website content on alumni.life.edu through Blackbaud’s NetCommunity, in partnership with Office of Advancement and University Marketing. Apply data analytics skills to report efficacy of communications in the Office of Advancement internally and externally. Administrator of project management software (i.e. Monday.com) for all Office of Advancement communication initiatives. Supports Alumni & Friends Department related to social media channels. Monitors industry trends and higher education advancement best practices to enhance communication effectiveness and constituent engagement. Serves as Executive Assistant to the Vice President of University Advancement, and the Associate Vice President of Development, Research and Innovation for a maximum of 10 hours per week Additional Duties And Responsibilities Ability to adjust to new projects, provide a strategic mindset and work in a fast-paced environment composed of digital and physical campaigns. Assist with special projects and initiatives as needed. Represents the Office of University Advancement in a professional manner consistent with the mission, values and standards of Life University. Demonstrates exceptional written and verbal communication skills. Supports a collaborative, service-oriented culture within University Advancement. Exhibits student centeredness in performance of all job duties. Uphold a strict level of confidentiality regarding donor, constituent and institutional information. Treats all others with respect and understands the impact of culture/background on the behavior of others. Respects differences among the Life community and demonstrates inclusive behavior. Anticipates, listens to, understands and responds to customer needs. Delivers work products and services to customers in a way that reflects positively upon the department and the University. Proven interpersonal skills with experience providing administrative support in a high-profile environment with tact and diplomacy, experience managing multiple deadlines and experience working with minimal supervision. Maintains neat, clean, professional appearance as directed by university policy. Additional duties and responsibilities as assigned. Qualifications Education, Training, and/or Experience Bachelor’s Degree in Communications, Marketing, Journalism, Public Relations, English or related field from an accredited institution of higher education, or similar; AND Minimum of two (2) to three (3) years of experience in a nonprofit, education, fundraising or communications setting. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in business, higher education or related field. Experience with Blackbaud, Raiser’s Edge NXT, NetCommunity, Monday.com, Canva, Microsoft Office Suite including Word, Excel, Power Point, Outlook, M365 Copilot or other Advancement and Stewardship focused CRM platforms and comparable tools. Three (3) to five (5) years of experience in a nonprofit, education, fundraising or communications setting preferred. Life University welcomes candidates with a variety of experiences and skillsets. If you are excited about this opportunity and believe your skills, experience and passion align with the role, we encourage you to apply even if you do not meet every requirement. We value transferable skills, a willingness to learn and a commitment to our mission. Physical Demands Nature of work requires the ability to operate standard business office equipment. Requires ability to communicate and exchange information, collects, compiles, compares, and prepares work documents, set-up and maintain work files. Must be able to lift up to 25 lbs; retrieving and placing materials on high shelves and on floor-level shelves; standing, walking; carrying; grasping; hearing; seeing; sitting; kneeling; climbing; balancing; stooping; crouching and reaching. Working Conditions Work performed in an executive office environment. May require availability for overtime hours during peak periods, including 4 or more weekend days per year. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    }
